didate> -- <the shared file>` and compare the actual rows before writing a word. Resemblance at the headline is not evidence of duplication, and neither is it evidence of novelty.** 🔢 **F-2491-1's weekly counter earned its keep for the FOURTH time and changed the filing before a word was written: `2026-W36: 18 standalone, 10 batched` against a budget of 3, so this went in ROUNDUP-CLASS rather than as a nineteenth headline.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: "are these two items the same news?" is a JUDGEMENT over prose, so a red would fire on every legitimate pair of related items and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate) — the same restraint the GZ-01 clause itself takes in forbidding a red guard on absent hashes. The cure is the sentence you are reading.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS for this streak: twenty-odd findings have asked how a SUBJECT SET can be wrong — empty, stale, narrowed, unreadable, mis-rooted, expired. This set is exactly right and its two members are CONFUSABLE WITH EACH OTHER. When a tool hands you a correct list and asks you to judge it, the failure moves from the instrument to the resemblance between items, and no widening of the selector can help.** Filed: item + dismissal at `marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md` head, merges `a15d3f020` (verdicts) and `db63956c6` (pointer re-base).

