🩺 **F-2498-1 (s2498, 2026-09-04) — `e4-dust-flats.spec.ts` ASSERTS AN ORPHANED IMPLEMENTATION, NOT A STALE INPUT CONTRACT; F-2497-1's PRESCRIBED CURE IS A MEASURED NO-OP AND F-2497-3 IS NOT INDEPENDENT OF IT.** s2497 filed `:97` as "presses Space expecting a road grade … the only thing between that test and green" and carried it as next-fire priority (B), a "test-only edit". **REPRODUCED FIRST (4 failed / 2 passed, `--workers=1`), INCLUDING s2497's OWN CONTROL — its account that the merge moves `:97` FORWARD (main dies at `:103` on `vehicle.active`, the merged tree reaches `:110`) is CONFIRMED.** Then the decisive probe, control asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1): `contract=e4-dust-flats vehicleActive=true` and **117 populated diagnostics keys**, so a null is an ANSWER and not a failed read — and `dustFlats` reads **`null` BEFORE any input, `null` AFTER the prescribed Upgrade, `null` AFTER Space**, with zero console errors. **No keypress can move a diagnostic that is never published.** ⚙️ **ROOT CAUSE, ONE NOT TWO: `src/world/DustFlatsTile.ts:131 diagnostics()` returns exactly the `{enabled, ringRoad, weather, orbit, roads}` shape BOTH failing tests assert, and that class has ZERO IMPORTERS** (measured: `grep -rn "from '.*DustFlatsTile'\|createDustFlatsTile" src/ e2e/ scripts/` returns nothing). `:31` reads the `undefined` directly; `:97` reads the SAME `undefined` behind `?? 0` and polls 0 forever. ⓘ **The codebase already said so in three places nobody reconciled the tests with** — `src/sim/MotorSocket.ts:29-31` (*"Today's `Game.ts` carries none of it: `DustFlatsTile` has no importer"*), `HeadlessContractSim.ts:691`, `MechanicsManifest.ts:338`. ✅ **AND THE CAPABILITY IS NOT LOST — IT WAS REBUILT ALONG ANOTHER PATH AND THE OLD ONE LEFT ORPHANED:** `e4-roads-and-convoys` `48ef7df8d` put the composition in `MotorSocket.ts`, `e4-vehicles-plain-boot` `98cc0fc2f` mounted it in a plain boot, and `Game.ts:9262 motorGrade()` calls `motorSocket.gradeAt(...)`, adds 