🧾🟢 **F-2495-1 — EVERY JUDGING TEST IN THE EVIDENCE SWEEP ASSUMES A *FINISHED* SUBJECT, AND ON A LIVE HEAT ITS SHARPEST INSTRUMENT DISCRIMINATES NOTHING (s2495, dry board)** — F-2487-1 mechanised F-2483-1's fifth test (*is this content already committed in another form?*) as blob identity against `refs/remotes/`, and rightly called it exact where prose equivalence is not. **It is — for a heat that has LANDED.** MEASURED s2495, the first fire to run this sweep MID-HEAT: `git worktree list` = 100 trees, `98` answered · `2` could-not-answer (the known prunable heat-7 pair, F-2485-1), each read's CONTROL asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1 — every answering tree returned 9k–25k TRACKED files, so a zero is an ANSWER and not a failed read). Result: **`119` untracked evidence-prefix paths in NO object database, across 4 sites — and F-2487-1's test scores all 119 identically AT RISK, because nothing in a live heat is committed yet, so the ANCHORED question returns “no” for every subject and separates none of them.** THE UNANCHORED QUESTION STILL WORKS AND NEEDS NO REFS — hash every subject and GROUP BY BLOB: **`86 of 119` paths (72%) are blobs living in ≥ 2 on-disk locations** (the arena writes a flat `artifacts/heat11/<rig>/<map>/` path and the wrapper mirrors it into the dated `artifacts/gauntlet-heat11-20260903/rides/<map>/<rig>/` home), leaving **`33` unique on disk / 3,687 KB**. **This CONFIRMS F-2487-1's staging-copy reading QUANTITATIVELY rather than overturning it** — that fire read a 99-file mapping by hand and said “almost always”; the ratio is now measured. AND EVERY ONE OF THE 33 IS IN FLIGHT, established by MTIME rather than assumed (the F-2483-1 method lesson, which s2482 and s2483 each got wrong on this very directory): repo-root heat mirror `28` — newest write **0.1 min ago**, `e5-flotilla/opus/wall.log`, a ride riding as I measured · live `/tmp/heat11-5e7a7c0b` arena `3` (that same unfinished ride's outcome + probes, not yet mirrored) · `worktrees/lane-c` `2` (`reviews/shots-e4-vehicles-plain-boot/{desktop,mobile}-chrome.png` — the in-flight runner's own output, which its delta commit carries). **NOTHING IS OWED AND NOTHING WAS TOUCHED.** SEVERITY HONEST AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, nothing at risk, NOT a false green — no instrument ever claimed these were safe, and the attended session is committing each ride AS IT LANDS (F-2492-1's measured convention, re-confirmed at HEAD: `wall.log` files read tracked-and-MODIFIED in my own `git status`). What earns it a line is the DIRECTION at the one moment it fires: a fire reading `119 at risk` mid-heat either salvages 86 duplicates as noise, or reaches into a live lane or arena to “rescue” them — the Mistake #2 direction F-2489-1 forbids in the same breath. CURE — a SIXTH judging test that narrows the five and retires none: **before judging a sweep result, ask whether anything is still WRITING it** (one `stat` for the tree's newest mtime). Still live ⇒ REPORT, DO NOT TOUCH, whoever owns it; quiet ⇒ F-2487-1's committed-ness test is the right instrument. NO GUARD, restraint INHERITED not re-argued: an untracked file in a live arena or lane is a LAWFUL routine mid-run state, so a red fires during ordinary correct operation and is excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate) — the same restraint F-2357-1, F-2389-1, F-2484-1, F-2485-1, F-2487-1, F-2488-1 and F-2489-1 all took for this very sweep. 💡 REUSABLE, A NEW AXIS: this streak has asked how WIDE the selector is (F-2358-1), whether its axis can EXPRESS the defect (F-2389-1), WHICH TREE it runs in (F-2484-1), whether a registry is a census (F-2485-1), how many declared subjects the author VISITED (F-2487-1/F-2488-1), and whether it counts ENTRIES or FILES (F-2489-1/F-2490-1) — **every one a question about the SUBJECT SET. This one is about the CLOCK.** A discriminator that is exact on a finished corpus can be VACUOUS on a live one, so before trusting one, ask what it returns while the work is still happening. Law: `scripts/fire.md` §2E (sixth judging test, appended to the F-2483-1/F-2492-1 block). Related: [F-2487-1], [F-2483-1], [F-2492-1], [F-2489-1], [F-2485-1].

⏳ **F-2492-1 (s2492) — F-2483-1 WAS RIGHT AND EXPIRED WITHIN THREE HOURS: ITS "DO NOT TRACK `wall.log`" RESTS ON A CONVENTION THE OWNER REVERSED WHILE IT WAS STILL THE NEWEST CLAUSE IN THE FILE.** F-2483-1 (landed s2483, ~23:49 on 2026-09-03) added a FIFTH judging test to the untracked-evidence sweep and answered it from a census: *"`git log --all --diff-filter=A -- '*wall.log'` returns ZERO — no `wall.log` has ever been added to this repo, across 18 heat directories"*. RE-MEASURED s2492: **`14` tracked `wall.log` files, added across `6` attended commits, the first at `9e56cc1e7` 2026-09-04T02:46:24+07:00** — about three hours later — **and the reversal includes THE EXACT TWO FILES F-2483-1 JUDGED** (`e1-twin-banks/{fable,opus}/wall.log`), both tracked today. The practice is deliberate and repeated, not a slip: the attended heat commits each ride's `wall.log` AS THAT RIDE LANDS, which is why my `git status` showed two of them TRACKED-and-MODIFIED mid-ride. SEVERITY HONEST AND NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, nothing lost, no verdict anywhere wrong, and F-2483-1's REASONING is untouched — its fifth test (*is this content already committed in another form?*) is still exactly the right question and the transport facts really are in `ride-meta.json`. What earns the correction is that the test was ANSWERED FROM A CONVENTION: a fire obeying the clause literally today would decline to commit evidence the attended session is actively committing, failing toward the RETENTION LAW's own loss direction (Mistake #11) in the very directory F-2484-1 and F-2487-1 spent whole fires salvaging. CURE (narrows the fifth test, does not retire it): "this repo has never tracked X" is EVIDENCE ABOUT THE PAST, never a rule for the present — re-check the convention AT HEAD with the same one-line `git log --diff-filter=A` before declining on convention grounds, and when the subject is a LIVE attended artifact the owner's own commits ARE the ruling. NO GUARD, restraint INHERITED not re-argued: