🧾🟢 **F-2490-1 — I CENSUSED THE CLASS F-2489-1 OPENED AND IT HAS EXACTLY ONE LIVE MEMBER, WHICH IS THE ONE ALREADY KNOWN — SO THE FINDING IS THE *NEGATIVE*, AND THE CURE IS ONE FLAG (s2490)** — s2489 proved `git status --porcelain` counts ENTRIES not FILES and handed forward *"nobody has asked which OTHER dirt census in this repo inherits the same collapse."* VERIFIED UNCLAIMED BEFORE SPENDING (my memory's own warning that an offered job may already be four clauses down): `0` occurrences in `CLAUDE.md`, `0` in `scripts/fire.md`, no successor row. MECHANISM VALIDATED FIRST RATHER THAN INHERITED (F-2215-1): `--porcelain` vs `--porcelain -uall` on the live trees gives lane-b `7 → 17` and **main itself `26 → 90`, a 3.46× collapse, today**. CENSUS RESULT — the class is a SINGLETON: of every dirt-reading site, `lane-runner-v3.sh:11` (the delta committer whose miss CAUSED F-2489-1's near-loss) already passes `--porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all`, and `art-staging-audit.mjs:439` (the RETENTION LAW's own alarm) already passes `--untracked-files=all` — **the two most consequential readers were immune by construction all along** — leaving `lane-usable.mjs` `dirt()` as the ONLY live member, exactly the one s2489 named. ⚠️ **AND THE OBVIOUS KEY IS ANTI-CORRELATED, WHICH IS THE HALF WORTH CARRYING: `--short` scores 6 hits and **5 are `git rev-parse --short HEAD`** — a different flag entirely (short HASH, not short STATUS) — while `--porcelain` scores hits that are `git worktree list --porcelain`, a different COMMAND, and `desk-state-audit.mjs`'s hit is a JavaScript property named `status`. A token sweep here is mostly false positives; the real key is the CALL SITE, read.** There is also no second collapse route: `git ls-files --others --directory` appears `0` times in the repo. SEVERITY HONEST AND NOT INFLATED: the VERDICT was never wrong — `untracked` is DISPLAY-ONLY (`lane-usable.mjs:505`,`:511` — re-measured AFTER my own edit, which shifted them +19; cite the CODE, the coordinate drifts) and drives nothing — so no lane was ever wrongly frozen or wrongly refilled, and this is NOT a false green. What earns the cure is that `clean -fd` deletes FILES, so the file count is the only number that answers *"what would a refill destroy?"*. CURED: `dirt()` now passes `--untracked-files=all`. PRICED, NOT FEARED — **+14% on this tool's git time fleet-wide (19.3s → 22.0s)**; reporting BOTH numbers was priced and REJECTED at **+50% (+10.4s)** for a read every fire runs at triage, and the entry count is the defective number nobody needs. DELTA MEASURED, NOT CLAIMED NEUTRAL (this cure is deliberately NOT behaviour-neutral): across the tool's own 30-row fleet **`0` ahead/verdict values move** and `3` untracked counts become truthful — **lane-b `1 → 21`, the F-2489-1 victim itself** — summing `5` entries → `43` files (8.60×); across the wider 99-tree registry the same call moves `12` trees, `215` entries → `3,925` files (18.26×), worst `gr-task-rehearsal` reading `untracked=4` for **2,738** real files. GUARDED by `scripts/lane-usable-untracked-files-guard.test.mjs` — 9 arms, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`, `gate-caller-audit` PASS. TEETH, 5 variants on scratch copies with the file restored byte-identical each time: PRE-CURE verbatim reds 4 · `-unormal` reds 3 · the over-general `--ignored` reds its OWN reverse control ALONE · the LAWFUL short form `-uall` correctly stays GREEN · broken git args red 7. ⚠️ **TWO METHOD NOTES PAID FOR IN THIS FIRE, both caught by controls rather than by reading. (1) A MANUFACTURED VARIANT MUST SATISFY ITS SUBJECT'S OWN MODULE-MAIN PREDICATE: `lane-usable.mjs:622` is a REGEX ON THE FILENAME, so my variant written as `.tmp-variant-xxx.mjs` never ran `main()` and exited **rc=0, 0 B stdout, no stderr** — indistinguishable from a subject that reported nothing. That is F-2215-1's silent-control trap with a new silencer: there a `/tmp` symlink, here a FILENAME. (2) MY FIRST REVERSE CONTROL ASSERTED THE WRONG BUCKET and MISSED the `--ignored` variant entirely: git prints ignored paths as `!! path`, and `classifyDirt` sorts only `??` into `untracked`, so `!!` falls through to the TRACKED bucket — **the bucket that DRIVES the DIRTY verdict**. The over-general cure was worse than it looked and the obvious control was blind to it.** 💡 REUSABLE: **a census framed on a TOKEN finds the wrong population; framed on the CALL SITE it finds the right one and is decidable by reading.** And a negative result is worth banking loudly — the answer here is *"the class is a singleton and your two most dangerous readers were already correct"*, which no future fire should have to re-derive. Law: `scripts/fire.md` §2E. Related: [F-2489-1], [F-2484-1], [F-1416-1], [F-2209-1], [F-2215-1].

🧾🟢 **F-2489-1 — THE PER-WORKTREE SWEEP EXCLUDES 30 REGISTERED TREES *INSIDE* THE REPO ROOT BY ITS OWN WORDING, AND `git status` COLLAPSED AN 11-FILE / 1.0 MB EVIDENCE DIRECTORY INTO ONE LINE SO AN ATTENDED SALVAGE WALKED PAST IT (s2489)** — F-2484-1 says *"for any tree OUTSIDE the repo root"*; F-2488-1 swept all 68 of those and nobody asked the 30 inside (26 `.claude/worktrees/agent-*` + the four lanes), while main’s own repo-wide `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` returns ZERO paths under either directory. MEASURED over all 30, each read’s control asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1; 21,290–25,493 tracked files per tree, so a zero is an ANSWER): 30 answered · 0 could-not-answer · 5 hold untracked content · 35 evidence-prefix paths · **15 in NO object database** — `lane-b/artifacts/e4-roads-and-convoys/` (11 files, 1.0 MB of gate logs, tapes and summaries) and `lane-d/artifacts/e8-mare-claim-physics/` (`prover.mjs`, `ride.mjs`, `probe-seams.mjs`, `probe-threats.mjs` — the CONTROLLERS that produce the proof). CAUSE MEASURED, NOT GUESSED: both lanes carry an attended `wip:` commit (*"salvaged attended during the API outage … resume from here"*) and BOTH contain ONLY tracked-file edits, 0 `artifacts/` paths between them — because `git status --porcelain` in lane-b prints **10 lines for 20 changed files**, the whole evidence directory being the single entry `?? artifacts/e4-roads-and-convoys/`. So a dirt count read from `git status` counts ENTRIES, not FILES, and the gap is unbounded; our own `lane-usable --all` inherits it, reporting `lane-b … untracked=1` for 11 files. LOSS PATH IS CODE, NOT CONJECTURE: `lane-runner-v3.sh:550` refreshes a lane with `git reset --hard main && git clean -fd`, and `clean -fd` DELETES untracked files — so this sits one refill from gone, protected today only by the temporary fence on line 1 (*"no refills into b/d until their leaves flip"*), which lifts exactly when those tracks finish. SEVERITY HONEST AND NOT INFLATED: **nothing was lost**, not a false green (no instrument ever claimed these were safe; none was asked, and `lane-usable` never claimed to count files), realised cost ZERO. CURED: all 15 salvaged with F-2484-1’s untouching method (hash FROM MAIN, throwaway `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, PARENTLESS `commit-tree`) to `save/lane-inflight-evidence-s2489` = `387ea0a91`, PUSHED; re-measured **AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0 · SAFE 35/35**, and untouchedness MEASURED on both sides (`git status --porcelain` = 19/10/1 before and after on main, lane-b, lane-d). NOT committed to main and NOT added into either lane — a `save/*` ref makes the bytes permanent and decides nothing; the tracks’ own drains still own their curated evidence. NO GUARD, restraint inherited (F-1460-1): untracked files in a live lane are a lawful routine state. REUSABLE — a NEW AXIS after F-2484-1 (*which tree?*), F-2485-1 (*a registry is not a census*) and F-2487-1/F-2488-1 (*declared vs visited*): **a summary view is a lossy projection, and `git status` is one.** Every prior finding in this streak had the wrong subject SET; this one has the right set and reads a COLLAPSED VIEW of it. Law: `scripts/fire.md` §2E.

🧾🟢 **F-2488-1 — F-2484-1’S PER-WORKTREE SWEEP DECLARES 68 SUBJECTS AND HAD ONLY EVER BEEN RUN ON 9; THE OTHER 59 HELD 93.6 MB OF DRAIN EVIDENCE IN NO OBJECT DATABASE (s2488, 2026-09-04, TWENTIETH CONSECUTIVE DRY BOARD).** F-2484-1’s rule is *"for any tree OUTSIDE the repo root, take the untracked read again"* — 68 trees. s2484 swept `heat11`, s2485 the 2 PRUNABLE, s2487 all six live `/tmp` arenas; **nobody asked the other 59**, because "arena" in every worked example quietly became the subject set. **MEASURED across all 68, each read’s CONTROL asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1 — every answering tree returned 9,906–25,488 TRACKED files): 66 answered · 2 COULD-NOT-ANSWER (the known prunable pair) · 46 hold untracked content · 284 paths under an evidence prefix, of which 179 are s2487’s cleared arenas and 105 had never been asked by anything — and 104 of those were in NO object database, aged 31–49 days, in three FINISHED attended `gr-task-*` worktrees:** `gr-task-e1-gameplay/reviews/shots-e1-depth` 83 files / 76.9 MB · `gr-task-digger/reviews/shots-e9-boss-old-digger` 8 / 10.1 MB · `gr-task-beauty2-far-ground/reviews/shots-beauty-pools/current` 14 / 7.3 MB. All are `reviews/shots-*` screenshots, the sink `CLAUDE.md` §4.1 names beside `artifacts/`. **THE PATH, NOT THE BLOB, IS THE DISCRIMINATOR — F-2483-1’s fifth test one rung up:** asking *has git EVER held this path, on any of 673 refs?* splits them into 14 superseded pre-merge files whose paths main does carry (the set `9ec7c4037` retained) and **91 (87.0 MB) at paths no ref has ever held**. Neither set is cited by any review, so `review-evidence-audit` is silent and correct to be (`ABSENT=17`, entirely disjoint), and the drains committed a curated subset — 88 shots on main against 83 left behind. ⚖️ **NOTHING WAS LOST and this is NOT a false green:** all 105 are on `save/attended-worktree-evidence-s2488` = `bfe5206cb`, parentless, PUSHED to origin (F-1055-1), re-measured **AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0 · SAFE 1