🔴 **F-2471-1 — THE BROWSER'S ERA REFUSAL IS UNREACHABLE FOR THE EXACT TAPE SHAPE IT NAMES, AND ITS GUARD IS RED ON MAIN TODAY (s2471, 2026-09-03; PRE-EXISTING, NOT the tape-resume slice — CONTROL-PROVEN).** `e2e/agent-reels.spec.ts:301` ("plain town board WATCH gives a half-stamped reel its honest unstamped-era refusal") FAILS on BOTH projects: it expects `data-era-refused="true"` and receives `"false"`, with the show reading `data-playback="playing"` — **the reel is PLAYED, not refused.** 🔬 **CONTROL, and it is what keeps this out of the drain's account: the identical failure with an identical fingerprint reproduces on `main`'s own worktree with none of the merged files present** (rc=1, 2 failed, same line 307, same expected/received). §3's "fingerprint-matched to known-reds with proof". 🔑 **DIAGNOSED BY READING, and the mechanism is exact and one line wide.** `src/game/Game.ts:7091` computes the refusal correctly — `!meta?.engineHash || meta.era !== engineEra.era || !engineEraIncludes(...)` — and is the ONLY site that computes it. The router seventeen lines above, `Game.ts:7033`, reads `if (hasAgentOrders && tape.meta?.engineHash && tape.meta.era)`. **A tape carrying an `engineHash` and NO `era` — precisely the "half-stamped" shape 7091 exists to catch — fails that guard and falls through to the LEGACY human-tape replay path, which never computes `eraRefusal` and simply plays the reel. The router and the refusal are complements that overlap wrongly: the gate diverts the case away from the only code that can judge it.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: this is NOT a ranking or data defect.** The door's server-side era filter (`functions/api/standings.ts`) is untouched and `test:stats` proves it green at 215/215 across both storage paths, so no unstamped reel can rank. The realised cost is **honesty on a player-visible surface** — the Lantern Show plays a reel that does not announce its era instead of showing the refusal the owner's 2026-08-31 era ruling promises — plus a **red sitting in a mandated e2e battery**, which is exactly how a red decays into one nobody investigates (F-1460-1). 🚫 **Deliberately NOT fixed in the drain: `src/game/Game.ts` and `src/ui/LanternShow.ts` are outside the tape-resume master's TOUCH-ONLY list, and a routing change on the true-reel driver needs its own gate.** ➡️ **PRICED AND FIRE-AUTHORABLE: the cure is one condition at `Game.ts:7033` (route on `hasAgentOrders` alone and let 7091 judge the stamp), and the e2e that must go green is ALREADY WRITTEN and ALREADY FAILING — so the corrective needs no new test, only the fix and its gate.** 💡 **REUSABLE: when a guard's condition and its ROUTER are written as complements, check the overlap rather than each half — a refusal that its own dispatcher can never reach is a refusal the factory does not have, and it reads as correct in every review of the file that contains it.**
🔴 **F-2467-1 — TWO ANSWERED OWNER QUESTIONS SAT ON THE DESK AS "AWAITING A WORD" FOR FOUR DAYS, AND TWO INDEPENDENT SELECTORS EACH CERTIFIED THEM OPEN — CORRECTLY (s2467, 2026-09-03, MEASURED, LIVE NOT LATENT, CURED AT THE LEDGER).** Found while reconciling a desk COUNT; it turned out to be a desk STATE error. **`F-SHOW-0830a`** (should the flagship boss punish static play?) and **`F-SHOW-0830b`** (the flagship reel reads fake) were **ANSWERED by the owner on 2026-08-30** — verbatim *"yes, all of this. lets improve this"* — **and the answer has fully SHIPPED**. 🔑 **TWO ORTHOGONAL MECHANISMS, BOTH BEING RIGHT: (a) POSITION OF THE CLAIM.** The closure was written into the F-SHOW-0830 row’s **BODY** (`✅ BOTH FORKS ANSWERED …`), and `desk-state-audit`’s subject-first rule reads only the first `90` chars — **deliberately**, because a body claim is not a state claim; the standing measurement that body closures run **~62.5% FALSE** is precisely why that rule exists. **(b) THE ID REGEX CANNOT EXPRESS THE ITEMS.** `FINDING_ONE = /\bF-[A-Z0-9]+(?:-[A-Z0-9]+)*-\d+\b/` requires a trailing `-<digits>`, so **`F-SHOW-0830a` and `F-SHOW-0830b` match NOTHING** and both collapse onto a single `F-SHOW-0830` row keyed to neither. Two honest tools partitioned on orthogonal keys, leaving a hole neither can report — **F-2358-1’s lesson exactly**. 👥 **THIS IS THE THIRD MEMBER OF F-2464-2’s FAMILY AND IS CITED AS SUCH RATHER THAN CLAIMED AS NEW:** that finding named (1) a closure tick behind another emoji (`lead.startsWith('✅')`, `0.19%` of rows) and (2) a compound desk heading hiding its second id. **This is (3): a desk id whose SHAPE the parser cannot express.** ⚖️ **The difference that matters is severity: F-2464-2 is LATENT and was filed priced. THIS ONE FIRED** — it kept two answered questions on the owner’s desk for four days. 🔎 **VERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY OF THE BODY TEXT, because that text is the thing under suspicion:** `specs/embodied-hand.md` is **Status: RATIFIED 2026-08-30**, quotes the owner verbatim, and **every one of its four slices has MERGED** — EH-1 `embodied-build-v2` @`a73790d9a2` (spec law 1 "one door, one hand": a walking hand cannot anchor-build, which is what **absorbs** the 0830a fork), EH-2 `true-reel-harness` @`8c5684def8`, EH-3 `true-reel-show` @`af85497537` (**this IS 0830b option (ii)**, the true renderer the owner asked for by name — *"can we not convert the AI tape to a human watchable tape?"*), EH-4 `gauntlet-heat7-embodied-crown` @`b43df480f3`. **Answered AND delivered**, not merely acknowledged. 🛠️ **CURED AT THE LEDGER, NOT AT THE PARSER** — the F-SHOW-0830 row now **leads `✅` with the bare id inside the 90-char zone**, so `desk-state-audit` reads it **CLOSED**, and both forks are **RETIRED from the desk s2467** with their original text preserved verbatim in place (Retention Law: mark, never erase). ⛔ **`scan()`/`FINDING_ONE` DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED, for F-2464-2’s own priced reason**: `scan()` is imported by `desk-state-audit`, `desk-carryforward-guard` and `ruling-propagation-guard`, and its guard is rooted in `test:node-guards` (**529.8 s floor, F-2166-2**) — which could not be run cleanly, because lane-a held a live gate battery for this fire’s whole duration and **F-2462-1** establishes that a self-contaminated battery manufactures findings. A ledger cure needs no code change and no battery. ⚠️ **MY FIRST EDIT WAS WRONG AND IS RECORDED BECAUSE IT IS THE LESSON:** leading the row with the SUFFIXED ids drove it from `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` to **`UNRECORDED`** — **strictly worse**, since the row lost its subject attribution entirely. **Reverted byte-identically** (`git checkout --`; baseline re-audited back to `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=2 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=48 · UNRECORDED=0`), then I **READ** `rowState`/`scan` (`findings-state-guard.mjs:81–111`) and rebuilt it correct by construction, with the splice REFUSING unless the bare id lands in-zone. **A remedy aimed by intuition at a selector you have not read is how a correct row gets corrupted.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOTHING WAS LOST and no owner question ever went unseen.** Desk ITEMS are carried by **SPLICE**, so both texts survived verbatim in every handoff and Robin could always read them; `CLOSED=0` was TRUE under the subject-first rule. The realised cost is that two **answered** items occupied desk space for four days and the headline over-counted. **It is NARROW: exactly `2` of `51` desk ids are inexpressible to the parser** — the other 49 were measured, not assumed. 🚫 **NO GUARD PROPOSED, and the restraint is measured rather than lazy:** *"is this body claim a real closure?"* is a **JUDGEMENT**, so a red would fire on every honest triage row that discusses an outcome and be excused into uselessness inside a week (**F-1460-1**, the `cross-engine` fate). It is the same restraint F-1669-1 took for done-move filenames. **The cure is the ledger row, at the site.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the sharp half:** the desk’s ITEMS are protected by splice; its **COUNT and its STATE are not**. A number carried by retyping is the one field that can drift, and a state written in a body is a state no instrument reads. **When a ledger row records an outcome, put it in the SUBJECT ZONE in the same commit** — a closure nobody’s parser can see is a closure the factory does not have. ➡️ **UNCLAIMED, AND EXACT:** sweep the board for 🔺/🎭-led rows whose BODY claims a closure (`ANSWERED`/`RULED`/`owner 2026-`) that their SUBJECT ZONE does not state. One grep plus judgement, no new tool. **Verify each against a RATIFIED artifact and shipped hashes, never against the body claim** — that is the ~62.5%-false population by construction.
🟡 **F-2468-1 — s2467’s INCIDENT WAS *NOT* F-2229-2’s PREDICTED RESIDUAL, AND THE DESK-SIDE RESIDUE OF ITS AIM (D) IS NOW EXHAUSTED BY MEASUREMENT (s2468, 2026-09-03)** — s2467 handed forward a "free and exact aim": sweep the board for 🔺/🎭-led rows whose BODY claims a closure their SUBJECT ZONE does not state. ⛔ **THAT SWEEP WAS ALREADY TAKEN — F-2362-1, s2362, over all 4,840 rows: 76 body-closure rows, 8 actively counted OPEN, and only 3 of those 8 genuine (62.5% FALSE), with a standing "do NOT re-take" attached.** What it could NOT cover is the population its own key is structurally blind to: `FINDING = /\bF-(?:[A-Z0-9]{1,8}-)+\d+\b/g` REQUIRES a trailing digit, so a letter-suffixed id matches **nothing at all**. 📊 **MEASURED s2468, corpus declared (F-2208-1): `tasks/BACKLOG.md` 5,176 lines / 7,523,715 B and the inherited desk line 38,118 B → BACKLOG holds 2,504 wide-distinct ids of which 2,488 are narrow-visible and **16 are letter-suffixed and invisible**; the INHERITED DESK holds 82 wide of which **exactly 2 are invisible — `F-SHOW-0830a` and `F-SHOW-0830b`, precisely the pair s2467 retired.** The desk now carries ZERO letter-suffixed ids and never carried a third, so the desk-side residue of aim (D) is EXHAUSTED — measured, not assumed.** 🔎 **All 16 were READ rather than trusted to the grep (the standing rule of this class): every one of the 7 `-s` forms is PROSE INFLECTION with no declaring row (`F-1600-1s` is the tail of "inside F-1600-1s OWN cure"), and the `-a`/`-b` forms occur inside F-2229-2’s own census prose. **That corroborates F-2229-2 at a new denominator** — it measured all 13 `-s` of 22 suffixed forms as inflections at s2229; I read 7 of 7 the same way today. ⛔ **THE CORRECTION, AND IT IS WHY THIS IS A ROW AND NOT A TICK: the obvious reading — that s2467’s incident IS the residual F-2229-2 predicted — IS FALSE.** That residual is *"a desk that routes a sub-id whose PARENT has no row"*, and F-2229-2 states it *"has never occurred in 1457 desks"*. **Checked against the pre-fix tree (`49a5488ff:tasks/BACKLOG.md`): the parent `F-SHOW-0830` row EXISTED and was 🎭-led OPEN. The clause stands UNFALSIFIED** — a fire citing s2467 as its counter-example would be filing a false refutation. 🔑 **THE ACTUAL MECHANISM IS A MODELLING ERROR, NOT A PARSER ONE, AND THAT IS THE REUSABLE HALF: the owner forked ONE question into TWO (a + b) and the ledger gave both ONE row — and a row is a SINGLE STATE-BEARING CELL.** With two answers and one lead the ledger did the only thing it could: it wrote both into the BODY, where the subject-first rule ignores them BY DESIGN. **Neither selector malfunctioned; the row was asked to hold a state it structurally cannot.** ➡️ **CURE, and it is a convention a fire can follow TODAY with no vocabulary change: when an owner answer forks a question, file TWO rows with BARE ids — never one row with suffixed desk tails.** Both states stay independently expressible and both ids stay regex-visible. 🚫 **Deliberately NOT a regex widening: F-2229-2 measured every widening arm as WORSE and says so in its own text, and changing census VOCABULARY is owner-gated (F-1336-5) while row flips are fire-executable.** ✅ **s2467’s cure VERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY rather than inherited (Mistake #4): `desk-state-audit --status <inherited desk>` reads `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=2 · BOTH=0 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=47 · UNRECORDED=0` = 49 — nothing is wrongly carried, and no id lost its attribution, which was s2467’s own near-miss when its first edit drove the row `UNRECORDED`.**


✅ **F-2465-1 SHIPPED (s2465, 2026-09-03, `d8db1520e`) — THE SPAWN-BOUND CENSUS CERTIFIED `0 EXPOSED INSIDE MANDATED LEGS` FROM A CORPUS THAT WAS MISSING NINE OF THEM, BECAUSE ITS COMMENT/STRING MASK HAD NO CONCEPT OF A REGEX LITERAL.** `spawn-bound-census.mjs`'s `codeMask` knew line comments, block comments and strings, and scanned a REGEX BODY as ordinary code — so a regex holding a quote character desynchronised it. `fixture-teardown.test.mjs:15` carries `(['"`])` inside `const PREFIX = /.../g`; the mask read that `'` as the start of a string and swallowed the rest of the file, including the real, UNBOUNDED `spawnSync(process.execPath, ['--test', ...])` at `:35`. 🔑 **THE DROP IS A SUBTRACTION FROM THE CORPUS, NOT AN ERROR — WHICH IS WHY TWENTY FIRES OF CURES COULD NOT SEE IT: there is no throw, no `catch`, no guard, no stale tree and no cwd. `unparsed` counts only `topLevelArgs` failures, never mask drops, so the site never became a row and its absence was indistinguishable from a clean board.** 📊 **PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING, WITH A REVERSE CONTROL: removing ONLY line 15's regex literal makes `:35` visible; removing an UNRELATED line leaves it hidden.** Corpus-wide the cure adds `26` occurrences and removes `2` — and both removals are genuinely inside a regex literal (`tmp-s2202-edge-semantics.mjs:117`), i.e. correctly hidden, so there are ZERO regressions. 🎯 **BLAST RADIUS, and it is the number the instrument exists to report: `9` genuinely-UNBOUNDED SYNC node-child spawn sites across `6` files, EVERY ONE inside a mandated battery leg — `dry-board-sibling-refusal-banner-guard.test.mjs:119` · `fixture-teardown.test.mjs:35` · `ledger-mirror-exposure-guard.test.mjs:215,216,235,242` · `no-emdash-scan-space-guard.test.mjs:92` · `probe-base.test.mjs:27` · `site-contract.test.mjs:147`. The cured census reproduces an INDEPENDENT hand-measurement exactly (9 sites, 6 files), by two methods that share no code.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOTHING REDS TODAY and no gate was ever wrong.** The census is ADVISORY (exit 0) and is chained bare in no battery; its one consumer, `triage-instrument-spawn-bound-guard`, is GREEN AND TRUTHFUL — it carries a proper anti-vacuity arm, and its subject set is exactly two triage instruments, neither affected. **What was false is the HEADLINE a fire reads**, and F-2436-1 cited that headline as one of three independent verifications that the F-2430-1 residue was zero. 🛠️ **CURE, three parts. (1) `codeMask` learns regex literals, with standard prev-significant-token disambiguation so DIVISION is not misread as a regex — the same defect with the opposite cause. It resyncs at a newline ON PURPOSE: a regex cannot span one, so a misread `/` costs ONE LINE instead of the rest of the file. Fail small, and in the direction that keeps code VISIBLE. (2) EXCLUDE PROPERTY ACCESS: surfacing those sites also surfaces `re.exec(src)`, `db.exec('create table …')` and `enemies.spawn()`, because `\bexec\s*\(` matches after a dot — false positives the old defect happened to hide. Measured: of `21` property-access spawner forms in this corpus, **ZERO** are a module-namespace `child_process` call, so nothing real can be lost; the day someone writes `cp.spawnSync` this must be revisited rather than widened by habit. (3) DECLARE BOTH EXCLUSION COUNTS on stdout ALWAYS, happy path included (F-2208-1) — the mask is the one place this census can narrow silently, so the narrowing is now a number that moved.** ⚠️ **AND THE BANNER WAS FIXED IN THE SAME BREATH, because the cure exposed it: the advisory verdict printed `✅` unconditionally, so it read `✅ 0 exposed` before the cure and **`✅ 9 exposed`** immediately after. In advisory mode stdout is the whole interface (F-2210-1), and a green tick beside a non-zero count is the exact false reassurance this instrument exists to prevent.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/spawn-census-mask-regex-guard.test.mjs` — 7 arms, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; `gate-caller-audit` PASS. FIXTURE-DRIVEN ON PURPOSE: a live-tree-only guard would go green the day someone deletes the offending regex, which would fix nothing about the mask.** 🔬 **TEETH, 5 variants on scratch copies with the subject restored VERBATIM (sha verified), and the sweep doubled as a reachability audit per s2226's duty: EVERY arm reds under at least one variant. Pre-cure mask reds 3 · property-access skip removed reds 1 ALONE · every-slash-is-a-regex reds the DIVISION control ALONE · dropping the declaration reds 1 ALONE · restoring the unconditional `✅` reds 1 ALONE.** ⚠️ **TWO METHOD NOTES PAID FOR IN THIS FIRE, both caught by my own controls rather than by reading. (1) MY DIVISION ARM WAS DECORATION AND THE SWEEP PROVED IT: the over-general variant reddened NOTHING, because my own newline-resync bounds a phantom regex to one line and my fixture put the division and the spawn on DIFFERENT lines. Same-line is the only parameterisation that can observe it. **A reverse-control sweep is also a reachability audit of your own new code — a manufactured defect that reds NOTHING is not a weak variant, it is a branch no test can reach.** (2) MY "the mask must still mask" FIXTURE WAS VACUOUS: `/spawnSync\s*\(/` contains no LITERAL `spawnSync(`, so the census's own needle never matched and the arm asserted `0 rows` for the wrong reason. It was caught ONLY by the companion `masked > 0` assertion — **when you assert that something is absent, assert in the same breath that it was ever present to be excluded.**

✅ **F-2465-2 DISCHARGED (s2465, 2026-09-03) — `fixture-teardown` HAS NO FAILING SUBJECT: IT IS NOT BROKEN, IT IS 116 FULL TEST-FILE RUNS DEEP, AND THE LAW'S "650 s" FIGURE IS STALE. s2464's DIAGNOSIS IS REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT.** s2464 handed this forward as next-fire priority (A), reporting that the guard "reds at the child-status assert (`:40`), i.e. some subject test FILE is failing" — with the subject's name lost to a truncated run. 📊 **SWEPT ALL `116` SUBJECTS by replicating the guard's exact method (same `mkdtemp`-using selection, isolated `TMPDIR` per child, `cwd=ROOT`, `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` deleted), collecting the full INVENTORY rather than failing fast: ARM 1 (child status) — `1` non-zero · ARM 2 (zero executed tests) — `0` · ARM 3 (fixture survivors) — `0` · zero-extractable-prefixes — `0`.** ✅ **AND THE ONE NON-ZERO WAS MY OWN BOUND, NOT A DEFECT — re-verified SERIALLY AND ALONE exactly as F-2462-1 requires, because the parallel pass ran 4-wide and contention manufactures findings: `gr-sim.test.mjs` run alone with an isolated `TMPDIR` and NO bound is `status=0`, **`326.2 s`**, `22 tests / 20 pass / 0 fail / 2 skipped`, `0` survivors. My sweep had killed it at 300 s.** ➡️ **SO NO SUBJECT FAILS, AND F-2459-3 / F-2460-3 / F-2462-5 ARE CLOSED FOR GOOD: ARM 3 reports `0` survivors across all 116 subjects, which independently confirms s2464's `art-staging-gitdir-link-guard` cure held.** ⏱️ **WHY IT LOOKED HUNG, AND THE FIGURE TO CARRY: this guard is ONE test that spawns a full `node --test` per subject, SERIALLY. Sum of children measured `869.9 s` (under 4-way contention), with `gr-sim` alone `326.2 s` — so a `>20 min` run is entirely LAWFUL. The "650 s when run alone" in `scripts/fire.md` predates the subject list reaching 116 and should be read as a FLOOR that only ever grows.** ⓘ **`--test-timeout` cannot rescue it either, and that is F-2429-1's own mechanism: `spawnSync` BLOCKS THE EVENT LOOP, so the outer timer can never fire.** ⚠️ **THE OPERATIONALLY IMPORTANT HALF, AND IT IS A NEAR-MISS I CAUGHT BEFORE SHIPPING IT: DO NOT BIND `fixture-teardown.test.mjs:35` AT `240_000`. F-2430-1's standard bound is BELOW this spawn's slowest LAWFUL observation (`326.2 s`), so applying the house constant mechanically would RED A LAWFUL RUN — F-1410-2 in the opposite costume, curing a hang by shrinking the bound until honest work fails.** ➡️ **THEREFORE THE 9 SITES F-2465-1 SURFACED ARE OWED WORK BUT ARE **NOT** A MECHANICAL SWEEP: each needs a bound measured against ITS OWN slowest lawful child. Eight of the nine spawn a short-lived CLI and `240_000` is generous for them; `fixture-teardown:35` needs a bound well above `326.2 s` and should be sized against `gr-sim` with headroom, re-measured rather than inherited.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is Mistake #4 pointed at a HANDOFF rather than at a stale board: a predecessor's DIAGNOSIS is a claim exactly as its verdict is, and this one was formed from a `| tail -25` pipeline (whose rc is the pipe's, as s2464 itself flagged) while a live lane battery contaminated the machine. **When you inherit "X is failing", re-derive the FAILURE before you spend a fire on the CAUSE** — the cheapest possible answer here was "nothing is failing", and it cost one sweep.**
🟡 **F-2464-2 — A CLOSURE TICK BEHIND ANY OTHER EMOJI IS INVISIBLE TO EVERY CONSUMER OF `scan()`, AND A COMPOUND DESK HEADING HIDES ITS SECOND ID OUTRIGHT (s2464, 2026-09-03, MEASURED, LATENT, FILED PRICED AND DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED).** Two independent selector gaps, found by asking whether the desk I inherited was still true. 🔬 **(1) POSITION, NOT PRESENCE.** `findings-state-guard.mjs:90` decides closure with `lead.startsWith('✅')` — so `⚖️✅ **F-WIN-2 RULED (attended 2026-09-03)**` is read as NEITHER closed NOR open, and `subjectState`'s `fallbackState` re-scan cannot rescue it because it applies the same test. The `struck` arm does not catch it either: that needs `/✅\s*(?:CLOSED|RETIRED)/`, and every one of these rows puts `**F-…` between the tick and the word. **PROVEN BY CONTROL, ground truth = an item the owner ruled TODAY: a desk carrying `F-WIN-2` alone reads `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` with evidence at the very row that rules it.** 📊 **CENSUS, so severity is measured and NOT inflated: of `2,089` BACKLOG rows whose 90-char subject carries an F-id, `390` lead with a bare `✅` and only `4` use the emoji-prefixed form — `0.19%`. This is a RARE house style, not a systematic hole.** ➡️ **THE CURE IS ONE LINE and its blast radius was measured before being recommended, not guessed: widening to `/^[^A-Za-z0-9\s]{1,6}✅/` flips EXACTLY `4` rows, and all four genuinely assert closure — the `F-WIN-2 RULED` row, the `human-tape-true-reel-stamp MERGED … F-SLHP-2 CLOSED` row, the `F-2456-1 — THE DESK LEADS WITH A 🚨 THAT IS DISCHARGED` row, and the `F-E3CF-4 CLOSED` row. Zero false positives. ⓘ **CITED BY CONTENT, NOT COORDINATE, AND THE FIRST DRAFT OF THIS ROW PROVES WHY: it named them `L6 · L19 · L71 · L1072`, measured minutes earlier — and then I prepended this very finding to the top of the file, shifting all four by exactly `+2` to `L8 · L21 · L73 · L1074`. The coordinates were WRONG AT THE MOMENT OF WRITING, before any later edit could rot them (F-2449-1: a pointer can be BORN drifted). Re-derive them with `/^[^A-Za-z0-9\s]{1,6}✅/` over the subject zone; the ids are stable and the line numbers are not.**** ⛔ **NOT SHIPPED THIS FIRE, and the restraint is priced rather than timid: `scan()` is imported by `desk-state-audit`, `desk-carryforward-guard` and `ruling-propagation-guard`, and its own guard `findings-state-guard.test.mjs` is rooted in `test:node-guards` (**529.8 s floor, F-2166-2**) — which could not be run cleanly, because lane-a held a live gate battery for this fire's whole duration and F-2462-1 establishes that a self-contaminated battery manufactures findings. **A green I could not trust is worth less than a finding I can.** The next fire on a quiet board lands it in one edit with this blast radius already measured. 🎯 **(2) THE COMPOUND HEADING, which is the half with a live cost today: the inherited desk carries one item headed `F-WIN-1 / F-WIN-2`, and `desk-state-audit` reports ONLY `F-WIN-1` — `F-WIN-2` is absent from its item list entirely, at any verdict.** So even after cure (1), a ruled id inside a shared heading stays invisible. ⚖️ **CONSEQUENCE, and it is F-1600-1 exactly — *a check that reports a discharged duty as owed reports it forever, and every fire pays the judgement cost again*: `F-WIN-2` WAS RULED by the attended session at `412836942` (option (b)) and the desk audit is structurally unable to say so.** ➡️ **WRITING RULE, which costs nothing and needs no code: give every desk id its OWN `🔺 **F-xxxx-x**` heading, even when two findings share one paragraph of reasoning. A heading is the audit's subject key, not decoration.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is this factory's most-repeated shape on a new axis: both gaps are selectors narrower than the question they are asked. The first keys on WHERE a marker sits rather than WHETHER it is there; the second keys on the FIRST id rather than every id. Neither can fail loudly, because in both cases the miss renders as the desk's ordinary resting state — `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` — which is exactly what a genuinely open item looks like.**

