** The tmpdir arms red on a **macOS sandbox refusal to scan the temp dir**, which has nothing to do with playwright collection; the whole-suite subdirectory arm reds because playwright run from `scripts/` **fails to find the config and sweeps `scripts/*.test.mjs` instead**. Three accidents and one real mechanism — so the sentence generalised a single subdirectory measurement onto tmpdir, where the cause is entirely different. ⛔ **AND THE STATED EXPOSURE WAS NOT ACTIONABLE AS WRITTEN, which is why it sat unclaimed for 149 fires: `nul-audit.mjs` and `attended-owed-audit.mjs` are NOT test files and cannot be run under `node --test`, so they could never have joined a list this guard feeds to `node --test`. They already carry their own dedicated guards (`nul-audit-corpus-guard`, `attended-owed-anchor-tree-guard`, `lane-usable-pathspec-root-guard`). The real exposure was the HARDCODING.** 🛠️ **CURE, in F-2207-1's inversion — enumerate what to SKIP so the set fails SAFE: the subject set is now DERIVED from an opt-in marker (`@cwd-invariant-collection-guard`) instead of transcribed, each subject ALSO runs from a repo SUBDIRECTORY (the cwd s2220 proved is dangerous, kept alongside tmpdir rather than replacing it), and an EMPTY subject set REFUSES instead of passing vacuously — a `for` loop over nothing registers no assertions and reports success (F-2217-1).** 🚫 **THE MARKER IS AN OPT-IN AND MUST STAY ONE, measured rather than stylistic: a content sniff (`/playwright/ && /--list/`) selects the guard AND its meta-guard, both of which merely quote list-mode, and the guard would then spawn ITSELF — the tautology this repo names in *"a pgrep liveness probe inside the command it probes"*.** ⚙️ **ONE IMPLEMENTATION NOTE WORTH MORE THAN THE CURE, because it is a trap in every meta-guard: the selector had to be EXTRACTED to a plain module (`scripts/collection-guard-subjects.mjs`), because `node:test` REGISTERS TESTS AT MODULE LOAD — so a meta-guard importing the selector from the guard's own test file also ran that file's five playwright arms. Measured: 11 tests / 5.26 s, of which 5 tests and 4.87 s belonged to the file it was only trying to read a function from, landing the SLOW battery's work inside the CHEAP one. After extraction: 6 tests / 0.46 s.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/collection-guards-subject-set-guard.test.mjs` — 6 arms, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; `gate-caller-audit` PASS.** 🔬 **TEETH, six variants manufactured on scratch copies, and the sweep doubled as a reachability audit per s2226's duty — EVERY arm reddens under at least one variant, so none is decoration: pre-cure verbatim reds 3,4,5 · drop the empty-set refusal reds **5 ALONE** · drop self-exclusion reds **6 ALONE** · drop the subdirectory cwd reds **3 ALONE** · a real subject losing its marker reds 1,2 · a runner that ignores subject failure reds **4 ALONE**.** ⓘ **All five predictions HELD this time — recorded plainly because the streak's running note has been that reverse controls keep repricing what their author was surest of, and one clean sweep is one data point against that, not a licence to stop building them.** ⚠️ **ONE GAP IN MY OWN FIRST DRAFT, found by the sweep and worth carrying: dropping the subdirectory cwd initially reddened NOTHING, because the fixture defect is caught by tmpdir too — so the arm I had just argued for was untested. Arm 3 now asserts BOTH cwd labels appear in the guard's output. A new parameterisation is not covered by a defect that any parameterisation would catch.** **ART-SLOT LAW (F-1045-1 + F-1044-4, written into law s1053 — both findings ordered it and neither had ever been written down): (1) any fire that TOUCHES the ART slot — refill, drain, or raws processing — ⏱️ **OR THAT FINDS A DRY BOARD — AMENDED s2159, executing F-2158-1's own priced recommendation.** The touch-trigger is structurally unobservable exactly when the slot is IDLE, and for retention **idleness is not the quiet period, it is the ACCRUAL period**: **583 files / 527