red s2487 by executing the three-fire-old cure across its whole subject set rather than admiring it).** s2484 swept `heat11` and salvaged it; s2485 found the `2` PRUNABLE trees; **neither asked the other FOUR live `/tmp` arenas anything at all.** 📊 **MEASURED s2487 over all six, with each read`s CONTROL asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1 — every tree returned 23,942–25,483 TRACKED files, so a zero is an ANSWER and not a failed read): `heat9` `0` untracked · `heat9-r2` `0` · `heat10` `0` · `gr-lane-d-edge` `2` (neither under an evidence prefix) · `heat11` `80` · **`heat8` `99`, an arena no sweep had ever reached** — 12 controllers, tapes and `jsonl` transcripts across six rig/map directories.** ✅ **AND EVERY ONE IS SAFE, ESTABLISHED IN TWO PROCESSES RATHER THAN ASSUMED: `99/99` and `80/80` are present in the object database AND reachable from an ORIGIN ref, so both prescribed buckets read `AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0`.** 🔑 **THE REUSABLE HALF IS A JUDGING TEST, AND IT MECHANISES THE ONE F-2483-1 DECLINED TO GUARD: that finding`s fifth test — *is this content already committed in another form?* — was declared a JUDGEMENT requiring you to read two files and decide equivalence, which is why no guard could express it. FOR ARENA RESIDUE IT IS NOT A JUDGEMENT. A detached arena SHARES main`s object database, so `git hash-object --stdin-paths` FROM MAIN plus a set-membership test against `git rev-list --objects` over `refs/remotes/` answers it EXACTLY, for thousands of files, in two processes — blob identity is decidable where prose equivalence is not.** ⛔ **BUT READ THE MAPPING BEFORE YOU BELIEVE THE HEADLINE, BECAUSE BLOB IDENTITY IS BLIND TO THE PATH AND I NEARLY PUBLISHED A CLEAN `99/99` OVER TWO REAL CAVEATS: of the 99, `94` match a same-basename file on main, **`1` IS AN EMPTY FILE** — where dedup matched an unrelated `artifacts/assay-e2e-20260822/replay-v2-control.err` and means NOTHING — and **`4` ARE CROSS-PATH WITH A SHIFTED ATTEMPT NUMBER** (arena `attempt-3.