 partitions on WHO DECLINED TO COMMIT IT — a key neither can express, and the only one under which the loss is visible. When a component REFUSES to do something, its refusal is a signal with an owner; ask who reads it.** **Report them, do not merely trust them — this audit has now shipped a false zero TWICE, both times because its headline was narrower than the question printed above it. (F-1054-1, fixed s1054 `4051bf31`): it checked only whether a staging file's NAME was absent from main, so 36.54 MB whose name matched main but whose BYTES were in no object database read as `0 files`; it now classifies by blob hash. (F-1055-1, fixed s1055 `c8034384`): "in git" was `cat-file -e`, which asks only THIS disk — so the same 36.54 MB, sitting on a local-only salvage branch whose push had timed out, again read `AT RISK 0`; every in-git blob is now also checked against the remote-tracking refs. If you find a third such gap, fix the class, not the instance.** 🕳️ **AND THE THIRD GAP WAS FOUND — IN THE CURE FOR THE THIRD FALSE ZERO, WHERE THE INSTRUCTION ABOVE SAYS TO LOOK (F-2216-1, measured and cured s2216 — the THIRTEENTH consecutive fire to find a live instance of F-2204-1's class).** The audit's step 2b — F-1184-5's cure, which asks `git diff origin/main..main -- assets/` for assets committed to main and never pushed — sat behind a **bare `catch`** justified by a comment reading *"no origin, or no origin/main remote-tracking ref yet — nothing to compare against, and a missing remote is already the loudest possible signal."* ⚠️ **BOTH HALVES ARE MEASURABLY FALSE, and the first one is the catch's OWN NAMED CASE: it fires when the REMOTE IS PRESENT and only the `origin/main` REF is unavailable — and then `offsite` is still populated from the other remote-tracking refs (137 on this repo), so NOTHING is loud. The unpushed files simply never enter `scan` and appear in no bucket at all.** It fires for any other failure of that one call too, which the comment never contemplated — F-2212-1's class exactly: a handler correct for its named cause and blind to every other one. 📊 **PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING on a scratch repo whose ground truth was ONE unpushed asset. Healthy git: `LOCAL-ONLY 1 files`, names it, `--strict` **rc=1**. Delete only `refs/remotes/origin/main`, remote and other refs intact: `LOCAL-ONLY 0 files`, `--strict` **rc=0**, `--json` `localOnlyFiles: 0` — ALL THREE MACHINE CHANNELS byte-identical to a genuinely safe board. Same for a transient failure of that one call.** The only dissent was an unlabelled line of **git's own stderr**, which no caller classifies and `--json` drops entirely — so per F-2211-1 it is not a signal, it is noise that happens to be true. ⚖️ **SEVERITY, STATED HONESTLY: on the live board the call SUCCEEDS, so every `LOCAL-ONLY 0` this streak has reported was TRUE — verified, not assumed. The defect is that the instrument is structurally incapable of telling you when it stops being true, and its consumer is not a gate but THIS LAW: the ART-SLOT duty makes every dry-board fire report that number to the OWNER, and seven consecutive fires have now reported it.** 🎯 **AND IT BEARS DIRECTLY ON AN OPEN DESK ITEM: F-2159-1 asks whether to root `art-staging-audit --strict` in `test:ledger-guards`. Answering YES before this cure would have rooted an arm that greens on its own blindness — a gate certifying the one thing it cannot see.** 🛠️ **CURE: DECLARE THE SOURCE'S COVERAGE, exactly as F-2196-1 declares the scan's BOUNDARY forty lines up in the same file — the corpus supplied the pattern for the FIFTH fire running. `mainTreeSource` is a STRING for F-2212-1's reason (a careless truthiness test on a failure value is TRUE, i.e. toward declaring), it discriminates `absent-ref` from `unverifiable` because those name two different owed acts (fetch/push vs investigate), it is printed on stdout **ALWAYS — including the happy path** since a declaration that appears only on failure re-creates the very ambiguity it removes (F-2208-1; the §4 desk-header precedent: if the desk is genuinely empty, still write the header), it is carried in `--json`, and `--strict` now separates **2 = "could not answer"** from **1 = "answered, and the answer refuses"** — the convention `drain-block-check`, `dry-board-probe`, `master-shipped-classifier` and `review-evidence-audit` already carry. **The advisory default still exits 0 by design, and this does NOT root the audit's `--strict` in any gate: F-2159-1 is the owner's question and a cure must not prejudge it.**  ✅ **BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2): stdout byte-identical but for the one new declaration line, rc unchanged in both modes, `AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0 · SALVAGED 797 files 600.08 MB`. Per F-2215-1 the control asserted its OWN validity first — "pre-cure arm produced 43 lines, it really ran" — because a control whose failure mode is silence cannot be told from the silence it measures.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/art-staging-local-only-source-guard.test.mjs` — 6 tests, 2.8 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; pre-cure reds 3 of 6, and each over-general cure is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it (collapsing 1 into 2 → arm 1 · declaring only on failure → arm 5 · refusing unconditionally → arms 1 and 6).** ⓘ **AND FOR THE FIRST TIME IN FIVE FIRES THE REVERSE CONTROLS DID NOT CORRECT MY PREDICTION — all four manufactured defects reddened exactly the arms I predicted. Recorded because the streak's running note has been the opposite; one clean prediction is not evidence the practice can be dropped, it is one data point against four.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the census question turned on a different axis: s2215 retired *"what does the TRY contain?"* in favour of *"what does the HANDLER do?"* — LOUD vs SILENT. That is right, and it found this site. But the polarity test is per-HANDLER while the harm is per-CONSUMER, and this handler has BOTH polarities at once: the same swallow makes `AT RISK` bigger (loud, self-announcing) and `LOCAL-ONLY` smaller (silent, a false zero). A handler is not sound because SOME caller notices; ask which number the LAW tells a fire to REPORT, and test that one.** 🔭 **AND THE `catch`-KEYED CENSUS IS ITSELF ONE INDIRECTION SHORT, MEASURED s2216: `spawnSync` NEVER THROWS on a failed child — it reports by RETURN VALUE — so s2212's *"46 non-test spawners with ZERO catch are structurally incapable"* is TRUE only for the throwing APIs. Measured: of 98 non-test scripts importing `child_process`, **63 use `execFileSync`/`execSync` (throw) and 28 use `spawnSync` (never throws), 18 of those with ZERO `catch` in the file** — a subject set every census in this streak has scored as incapable BY CONSTRUCTION. **Swept: all but one test `.status`, and that one is low-stakes (`gen-audio.mjs:194` reads `afinfo` stdout without testing either field, though it degrades to `null` rather than to a wrong number). The live decision instruments on this axis are SOUND and worth copying — `drain-block-check.mjs:320` (**was `:292` s2262–s2332 — re-based s2333, +28, when the F-2333-1 detached-HEAD refusal landed ~30 lines above it: the THIRD rot of this coordinate and the THIRD RUNNING caused by a fire editing the very script the law cites, predicted by this clause and cured in the same landing commit. Re-grepped, NOT arithmetic — the sibling pointer in this same file moved +76 in the same commit, so one remembered delta would have been wrong for the other**; was `:277` s2224–s2246 — re-based s2247, +15, when the F-2247-2 retired-reason-class exclusion landed above it; was `:212` s2216–s2223; re-based s2224, +65, when the F-2223-1 corpus-tree discriminator landed above it) is F-2212-1's own cure, and `red-inventory-lookup.mjs:64`/`:234` both test `.status` and degrade to `null` / an explicit `SNAPSHOT main commit UNKNOWN` line.** So this axis is clean TODAY, but it is not covered by the polarity test and the next fire should not assume it is. ⚠️ **AND THE POLARITY TEST HAS THE SAME BLIND SPOT EVERY CENSUS BEFORE IT HAD — MEASURED ON MY OWN NUMBERS, NOT PREDICTED. s2215 wrote that asking *what does the HANDLER do?* "needs NO reachability analysis, so it CANNOT be blind to an indirection BY CONSTRUCTION." That holds for the TRY side and FAILS for the HANDLER side: deciding whether a handler is LOUD means resolving what its calls DO, and a `process.exit` behind a one-line same-file helper is invisible to the token test.** 📊 **Measured s2216: of the `75` handlers the raw polarity test calls SILENT, **`4` ARE FALSE SILENTS** — `red-inventory-lookup.mjs:226`/`:256` call `fail()` (`process.exit(2)`), `blocker-panel-closed-guard.mjs:91`/`:113` call `refuse()`. TRUE SILENT after one pass of same-file wrapper resolution: `71`.** 🔑 **Two of those four are the exact coordinates s2215's handoff named as unexamined SILENT sites to sweep — so the aim I inherited pointed at two handlers that were already loud, and I found out ONLY because `law-pointer-guard` reddened on my citation of `:226` and made me read the line.** ⓘ **A guard caught a false accusation before it entered the law: that is the s1301 citations-run-LAST duty paying for itself, and it is why the coordinates above are `:64`/`:234` and not the ones I first wrote.** 💡 **So the ladder is NOT terminated, it has changed SIDES: file → lexical → same-file wrapper → imported helper, all on the TRY — and now wrapper resolution on the HANDLER. Resolve one level and re-count. Note too that my own cure ADDED a handler to this census (`102` → `103`), so a fire that edits a spawner moves the denominator it is measuring.** `worktrees/art/` is NOT a git worktree (no `.git`, absent from `git worktree list`), so its output is untracked-by-default and dies with the disk: F-1045-1 found **10 files / 16.5 MB** sitting in no commit, the oldest for **14 days**. That is a standing property of the slot, not one bad batch, and it is the RETENTION LAW's largest live hole. (2) Any ART refill must **cite the BACKLOG line proving the batch is unshipped** in the queued task or the handoff — art batches have been re-queued against already-shipped rosters (Mistake #8 shape).** 🧭 **AND BEFORE YOU SPEND AN AUTHORING BUDGET, ASK THE INSTRUMENT WHETHER ANYTHING IS AUTHORABLE AT ALL: `node scripts/authorable-candidates.mjs` (F-2153-1, measured s2153 — the tool has existed since F-1654-1 and THIS CLAUSE HAS NEVER NAMED IT).** It reads each `planned` leaf's structured `authoringBlock` (`class` / `finding` / `measuredBy` / `reason`), prints the refusal with who measured it and when, and closes with a census. **Measured s2153: `12 planned — 12 priced, 0 unpriced (owner-gated 8, attended-owed 3, needs-spec 1)` — i.e. ZERO fire-authorable**, so §2E's two-master dry-board allowance had nothing to spend itself on, and that is a FACT the tool states in one command rather than a judgement each fire must re-derive. ⚠️ **THE IRONY IS THE FINDING: the tool F-1654-1 built precisely so fires would stop re-deriving priced negatives is named in ZERO law surfaces.** Measured s2153 — `scripts/fire.md` **0** · `CLAUDE.md` **0** · `.claude/skills/author-task/SKILL.md` **0** · `.claude/skills/drain/SKILL.md` **0**; it appears only in `STATUS.md` handoff archives and `tasks/BACKLOG.md` findings prose, **the two surfaces F-1654-1 itself proved a refilling fire does not read at refill time.** So F-1654-1's own diagnosis — *"a measured refusal had nowhere to live"* — recurred one level up: **the refusal-READER had nowhere to live.** 💰 **Cost, paid by the fire that wrote this clause and not inherited from anyone: s2153 re-derived `jumper-8way-wiring`'s refusal BY HAND through six probes** — goal-tree status census → `master-shipped-classifier` → reading the master → grepping `assets/LEDGER.md` for the `char.claim_jumper SHEET full-ROTATION` row → `drain-block-check` → an `authoringBlock` census — to arrive at precisely the verdict s1661 had already recorded ON THE LEAF **eleven days earlier**, one command away. ⓘ **AND `drain-block-check` WILL NOT SAVE YOU HERE — IT PRINTS `✅ CLEAR` FOR BOTH BANKED MASTERS** (`lane-c-jumper-8way-wiring.md` and `lane-e3-fairground-socket.md`, verified s2153), and it is RIGHT to: it answers *may I DRAIN this?*, and a `planned` leaf has nothing to drain. **A CLEAR from the drain guard is not a licence to QUEUE** — the two questions have two instruments, and §3.0's tool is deliberately blind to `authoringBlock`. Its sibling `node scripts/master-shipped-classifier.mjs` answers the other half — *is this banked master already SHIPPED?* (Mistake #8, the 824k Flail) — and is likewise named in no law surface (`fire.md` 0 · `CLAUDE.md` 0 · `author-task/SKILL.md` 0, measured s2153). ⚠️ **AND RUN IT FROM THE MAIN WORKTREE — FROM A LANE IT USED TO INFLATE THE QUEUE-ME SET 268× AND SAY NOTHING (F-2222-2, measured s2222, CURED s2223).** Three of its four inputs are TRACKED (`tasks/*.md`, the trace dirs under `tasks/`, `tasks/goals.json`), so a linked worktree hands it a board FROZEN at that lane’s commit. It now REFUSES there (`⛔ CANNOT VERIFY — DO NOT QUEUE`, `--strict` 2) instead of clearing. **Read the refusal, do not re-run it somewhere else until it goes green.** ⚠️ **AND THAT CLASSIFIER COMPUTES ITS QUEUE LICENCE FROM TWO CORPORA WHILE DECLARING ONLY ONE — THE SECOND WAS UNDECLARED FOR SIX FIRES AND IS WORTH TWO ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE MORE THAN THE FIRST (F-2219-1, measured and cured s2219 — the SIXTEENTH consecutive fire to find a live instance of F-2204-1's class).** `verdictFor` builds SHIPPED from review evidence AND goal-leaf evidence. F-2213-1 cured the reviews arm into `mainReviews() -> {ok, source}` and wrote the reason at the site — *"a caller that reads CANDIDATES without reading this is reading a queue licence off an unknown source"* — and **seventeen lines below it the goal-leaf arm stayed a bare `existsSync(p) ? goalLeaves(JSON.parse(readFileSync(p))) : []`.** Nothing throws on that path, so **every catch-keyed census in this lineage (s2212–s2215) was structurally incapable of seeing it: the swallow is a GUARD, not a handler** (F-2218-1). 📊 **BLAST RADIUS BY CONTROLLED EXPERIMENT ON THE LIVE BOARD — same root, same 1125 masters, same reviews, the ONLY variable is this arm; both arms asserted their own validity first (F-2215-1), each having classified all 1125: goals read → `SHIPPED 704 · NO-TRACE 66 · CANDIDATES 1 · DISAGREES 97`; goals empty → `SHIPPED 547 · NO-TRACE 85 · CANDIDATES 8 · DISAGREES 272`. 157 masters out of SHIPPED and an 8× candidate inflation, INTO the set the tool exists to compute — the Mistake #8 polarity, same DIRECTION as F-2213-1 and two orders of magnitude larger in SIZE: that finding was cured on a blast radius of ONE flip.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY: LATENT, like F-2212-1/F-2213-1/F-2214-1 and unlike F-2218-1 — `tasks/goals.json` is TRACKED and was measured present in main and all four lane worktrees, and a MALFORMED file already refuses loudly through F-2214-1's catch. Only ABSENCE reaches the ternary silently. The defect is not that absence is likely; it is that the tool could not tell you which corpus its licence came from while its sibling arm had been saying so since s2213.** 🛠️ **CURE: `goalEvidence()` returns `{ source: 'goals' | 'absent', leaves }` — a STRING for F-2212-1's reason — carried in `--json` ALWAYS including the happy path (F-2208-1), with the human channel printing only a DEVIATION to match this file's own `reviewsSource` convention. `absent` DECLARES AND DOES NOT REFUSE (F-2218-1's restraint): a root without `goals.json` is LAWFUL — it is what all 12 legacy fixtures use and how `mainReviews` already treats a non-git root — so refusing there would red every fixture and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1). The parse path is DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE; re-coding a working cure in passing is a drive-by.** ✅ **BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2): all four modes `4/4` byte-identical on stdout and stderr, rc unchanged.** 🔒 **`scripts/master-shipped-goals-source-guard.test.mjs` — 8 tests, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; pre-cure restored verbatim reds 4 of 8 with both reverse controls green.** ⚠️ **A REVERSE CONTROL CORRECTED MY PREDICTION for the first time in three fires: I expected *refusing on `absent`* to red control 5 alone; it reds FOUR arms (2,3,4,5), because arms 2–4 read the absent-state classification a refusal replaces with a banner. Benign — over-coverage, not under — but recorded, because the streak's recent note has been that predictions hold, and one clean fire is not evidence the practice can be dropped.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is an AIMING rule rather than another census shape: A CENSUS'S DECLARED LIMIT IS THE MOST VALUABLE THING IN A HANDOFF — WORTH MORE THAN THE SITE IT NAMES.** s2218 handed over a hedged target (`art-staging-audit.mjs:373`, still unmeasured) *and* an admitted blind spot (*"my census is lexical and single-line"*). **Widening the census on that admission — multi-line guards as well as single-line ones — took its `6` sites to `13` single-line plus `4` multi-line, and found a live one in NEITHER list, because widening changed which FILES were subjects at all, not merely which lines.** When a predecessor tells you what their instrument cannot see, go there before you go to the site they named. ⚖️ **A priced leaf is NOT a closed one** — the tool prints that caveat itself; the price estimates the AUTHORING cost and never renders a verdict on the goal. If the ladder has nothing ready for an idle lane, **AUTHOR the next master yourself** (idle-fire authoring precedent: s41 m3-02, s42 m4-02) — but ONLY from an existing spec slice plus its evidence chain (predecessor's review file, audit verdicts, playtest findings — read them, quote them in the task). Follow the house task pattern (goal / scope / firewall / self-check, gates, sequencing laws), mark the header **FIRE-AUTHORED (attended review welcome)**, max one authored master per fire, no drain-budget cost — ⚖️ AMENDED (owner 2026-08-09, F-1511-5 ruling "Allow 2 masters when dry"): when the board is DRY (no drain existed this fire) and ≥2 lanes sit idle, the cap is TWO authored masters in that cycle; the cap protects quality, not idleness. HARD LIMIT — never invent scope: if the lane's next work has no spec slice, needs a design fork, or bends canon, do NOT author — flag **PIPELINE-DRY: <lane> (needs spec/owner)** in your handoff instead. Refills are non-drain actions (no budget cost). **MAIN THROTTLE (s72 lesson, 2026-07-06): while ≥3 undrained done-moves are waiting, do NOT refill the main queue beyond one small corrective — every main task holds the working tree dirty and blocks ALL lane merges. Drains outrank main throughput; re-queue paused main items (queue-paused/) once the pile is below 2.** 📮 **DISPATCH ORDER IS A LAW, NOT A HABIT — COMMIT THE MASTER AND ITS EVIDENCE FIRST, REFRESH THE LANE SECOND, `cp` THIRD, AND RUN THE MASTER'S OWN CITATION GREP BETWEEN 2 AND 3 (F-1424-3, measured s1424; folded in s1426 after being deferred one fire for a lane collision that has since cleared).** s1424 cured lane-c *before* committing the master, so the lane sat **exactly one commit behind** — the commit carrying the citation the master tells the runner to grep. The runner claimed the slot inside a minute and STOPPED: **44,007 tokens, zero files touched, zero work lost**, saved only because that master wired the grep as a hard STOP. ⚠️ **Curing the message could never have prevented this** — the fault is ordering, and no instrument was being asked about it. ➡️ **AND THE KEY ITSELF MUST BE PROVED BEFORE IT IS WRITTEN DOWN: grep the candidate span against the SOURCE FILE ON MAIN first — if it does not match *there*, it is not a key, it is a paraphrase (F-1425-2).** F-1310-1 says cite by CONTENT because coordinates rot; what neither clause said is that **`grep` is line-oriented and prose wraps**, so a key spanning a line break matches **nowhere, including in the file it was copied from**. s1425 caught this on its own dispatch: the key returned 0 in the lane and its first instinct was a stale lane, but `lane-usable` read `ahead=0 behind=0` and the same grep returned **0 against main too**. That failure is nastier than staleness because **the master specifies 0 to mean "the lane drifted"** — a false STOP whose error message accuses the wrong subject, sending the next fire chasing a phantom refresh. ⓘ **This is not a rare shape: s1426 hit it again while authoring, and all three of its first-draft keys returned 0 on main** — the fire had written the review file itself minutes earlier and its own prose still wrapped. Prefer a span that visibly sits on one line, verify **1 on main**, then verify **1 in the lane** after the refresh, and only then `cp`.
