scripts/tmp-s1143-goal.mjs:21:  authorNotes: 'FIRE-AUTHORED s1143. Test-only, src/** barred. RE-MEASURED AT SOURCE THIS FIRE, not inherited: e2e/vp-02b-rotation-resolver.spec.ts on current main is 1 failed / 6 passed (desktop-chrome, 1.6m), and the failure is a 30s TIMEOUT at :283 waiting for spriteAnimations[char.claim_jumper].loaded === true -- so the shape assert at :285 is NEVER REACHED and the test has never actually observed a jumper. Cause already diagnosed by an earlier slice, reviews/vp-02d.md:26: spawnPack() exposes char.bandit_base, not char.claim_jumper. This is a KNOWN pre-existing red (tracked as vp-02b :113 and :233, both fingerprinted in reviews/vp-02d.md), not a new one -- verified before authoring rather than claimed. The same slice closes F-1132-7, whose residual is named on the face of the guarded task 025: the 8-way jumper behaviour SHIPPED via the walk8 route (Enemy.ts:198/:753/:755 + grab/flee at :888/:894, all five verified at source this fire) and what is missing is TEST COVERAGE, not behaviour. Task 025 itself is guarded DO-NOT-QUEUE and is to be read, never queued or edited. Scope 1 is a measure-first STOP gate (find empirically which __GR_TEST__ surface mounts the slot; spawnThief is the hypothesis, NOT asserted as fact) and flags the KeyP pause at :235 as a candidate confound. Scope 3 explicitly licenses the runner to contradict the premise: if the jumper still shows the OLD six-key shape, keep the assert and report that task 025 overstates what shipped -- either outcome is a success. Scope 4 requires a mutation control, because a test that passes while silently observing nothing is the exact defect being cured. LANE-SAFETY pre-proved: git log main..lane/m4 shows one commit 5e9eba91, which s1142 DRAINED to main as 8cab8791 by tip-graft (done-move shipped-8cab8791-..., reviews/vp02-capture-error-surface.md on main) = false-ahead safe dupe.',
scripts/tmp-s1144-line1.txt:1:Last updated: 2026-07-28T00:07Z s1144 handoff, lock CLEARED — **NO DRAIN WAS AVAILABLE, AND THAT WAS THE FIND: THE ONE DONE-MOVE ON THE BOARD WAS A LAWFUL STOP WHOSE REFUSAL EXPOSED A 15-DAY-OLD RENAME NOBODY HAD PROPAGATED.** (A) ⛔ **NOT A DRAIN — `lane-vp-02b-jumper-slot-red` STOPPED LAWFULLY at its own scope-1 measure-first gate** (run `20260727-234321`; zero diff; `main..lane/m4` **EMPTY**). Recorded, not merged: done-move renamed `stopped-lawful-s1144-scope1-gate-fired-…`, goal leaf → `status:"stopped-lawful"`, **NO mergeHash** (unfinished work carries none), review `reviews/vp-02b-jumper-slot-red-stop.md`. ✓ **The runner was RIGHT and I re-derived its claim at source rather than inheriting it — a well-argued STOP is still a claim.** (B) 🔑 **F-1144-1 — ROOT CAUSE: `82543f27` (2026-07-12T21:32, `runner(lane-d): wire-e1-bandit-variants`) LEFT A RENAME HALF-DONE.** It rewired the enemy `SpriteAnimator`s at `src/entities/pools.ts:337`/`:355` from `assetSlots.charClaimJumper` to `charBanditBase`/`charBanditThief`, added both slots to `characters.v2.json` — **and updated ZERO of the seven e2e specs naming the old slot**; `git log -G"charBanditBase" -- src/entities/pools.ts` returns **exactly that one commit**. `spriteAnimationDiagnostics()` (`SpriteAnimator.ts:208`) is keyed **per constructed animator**, so `char.claim_jumper` can never be a key and the predecessor master's `spawnThief` hypothesis was **unfalsifiable by construction** — no surface could ever have satisfied it. ✓ **NO art/gameplay regression — I checked before blaming the runtime:** `char.bandit_base` carries `walk8:true` and its `char-bandit-base-sheet-walk8-*.png` are on disk; the enemy got **new** art and `enemy-claim-jumper.png` is now the encyclopedia portrait only. **The runtime half of `82543f27` was correct and complete; only the e2e layer was stranded.** The stranded set is **SEVEN specs** (`066-walk8-engine`, `lane-c-activations-assay-office`, `task-031-anim-roundness`, `task-042-anim-smoothness`, `visual-polish-assets`, `vp-02-sprite-animation`, `vp-02b-rotation-resolver`), and successive drains fingerprinted them **one at a time** as separate "pre-existing known reds" (`reviews/vp-02d.md:26`, `reviews/vp-02e.md:60`, `reviews/vp-02e-runner-report.md:81`/`:108`) **for 15 days** without joining them to one cause — the *fix-the-class-not-the-instance* law failing in slow motion. ⚠️ **`reviews/066-walk8-engine.md:24` records `claim_jumper now walk8 — pass ×2` but is dated 2026-07-10, TWO DAYS BEFORE the rename**: a stale green describing a tree that no longer exists. (C) 🔬 **F-1144-2 — TWO STALE CLASSES, AND CLASS A MASKS CLASS B.** Measured by me this fire (`--project=desktop-chrome`, port **5188 verified free**, all six queues empty, no runner live — Mistake #12): batch of the four unmeasured specs = **4 failed / 1 passed (1.0 m)**. **Class A (hero walk4→walk8):** `task-031:202` `hero.frameCount` **Expected 4, Received 8**; the same wait 30 s-times-out at `task-042:59` and `066:81`. **Class B (the rename):** `visual-polish-assets:68` `char.claim_jumper` → **"missing"** (expected `"loaded"`); `vp-02b:283` + `vp-02:705`/`:739` time out on the jumper wait. 🔑 **Class A fails FIRST in three specs, so they never reach their jumper asserts at all** — curing Class B alone will not green them, and curing Class A will *unmask* three more Class-B failures. **A red at row 1 says nothing about rows 2..N**, which is exactly why I split by failure LINE before claiming a class. (D) ✍️ **AUTHORED + QUEUED `lane-vp-02b-jumper-slot-repair` → lane-b, AND THE RUNNER HAS ALREADY PICKED IT UP** (run `20260728-000441` live; master↔queued byte-identical; `^CODEX:` **column 0, line 5**; goal leaf same commit `f6864768`; `task-guard-audit` **663 masters, 0 invisible, rc=0**; `drain-block-check` **CLEAR**). **Scope is Class B ONLY** — mechanical and verifiable. **Class A is deliberately EXCLUDED and routed to the OWNER'S DESK:** whether the hero being walk8 is the intended shipped state or a regression is a **design fork**, and `066-walk8-engine:200-205` asserts `.not.toContain('walk8')` **on purpose** — that is not a fire's call to settle. `visual-polish-assets` is written as a **STOP-and-report judgement, not a rename**: it is a **boot canary**, so a blind substitution could turn a real guard into one asserting a falsehood — the runner must first measure whether `char.bandit_base` is itself loaded in a plain boot, and is forbidden to weaken it. **Scope 5 warns that asserts unexecuted since 2026-07-12 may surface TRUE reds and explicitly licenses reporting one over greening it** (incl. `vp-02b:285`'s six-key shape, which task 025's `## e2e` item 4 anticipated flipping). Scope 6 demands a mutation control — *a test that passes while observing nothing is the defect being cured.* `tasks/025-vp-02e-jumper-8way-activation.md` stays ⛔ DO-NOT-QUEUE (read, never queued). (E) ➡️ **NEXT FIRE, IN ORDER: (1) DRAIN `lane-vp-02b-jumper-slot-repair`** when lane-b done-moves — **the bar: the before/after table for all seven specs WITH first-failure lines; base-vs-thief justified per call site; scope-3 resolved (substituted with proof, or STOPPED with numbers — a stop there is a success); the scope-6 mutation control shown RED then restored byte-exact; zero `src/`. ⚠️ THE THREE CLASS-A SPECS (`066`, `task-042`, `task-031`) WILL STILL BE RED AT THEIR CLASS-A LINE — THAT IS EXPECTED AND PRE-DECLARED, NOT A FAILURE. If the runner reports a NEW true red behind a repaired wait, that finding OUTRANKS the green.** **(2)** F-1144-2 Class A (hero walk4-vs-walk8) → **owner's desk, do not author a pick.** **(3)** F-1143-1/F-1143-2 census brightness + the non-asserting `FAIL:` cells — owner-gated, unchanged. **(4)** F-1141-3 mobile HUD overlap owner-gated. **(5)** F-1140-3 `:146` load-sensitive at 25%. **(6)** `m3-05 run-history` still needs its re-scope. **(7) Still unblocked and unauthored** (my one-master cap went to the repair): the **trail-guide residue** of two uncovered triggers, *first B-open* and *first theft alarm* (F-1133-1) — not an owner decision per BACKLOG, but it needs **new player-facing copy**, which is why three fires have now left it. **(8) Owner's desk, unchanged and not re-litigated:** F-1144-2 Class A (new) · F-1143-1/2 · F-1141-3 · F-1141-2 · E① pathing cure (F-1131-5) · E② F-1130-6 · F-1131-1 · `F-1123-4` · `town-t1-square:96` (F-1114-1) · the ~300-file `artifacts/` churn sweep (untouched again; path-scoped adds only). ⚠️ **PIPELINE-DRY: lane-a, lane-c, lane-d, main, art — and this time it is PROVEN, not inherited:** a non-terminal goal-leaf query returns **exactly 3 of 144** leaves, and I named why each is parked — `rf-34-hero-y-restore-roundtrip` (owner design fork F-1096-2, one word unblocks) · `calibrate-suite-workers-v2` (owner-gated s1125; the BOX is the blocker, lifts ranked 1-4 in its blockedReason) · `lane-vp-02b-jumper-slot-repair` (mine, live on lane-b). **Report-only findings banked for a later slice (`src/**` barred in the queued task):** `src/assets/generated.ts:206` still names `charClaimJumper` **boot-critical** though it measures `"missing"` in a plain boot; `src/entities/pools.ts:343`/`:349` batch names still read `GeneratedClaimJumperThief…` — **that vestige is precisely what hid the rename for 15 days.** (F) 🧾 **Duties, stated not skipped: NO GAZETTE ITEM — nothing merged this fire, so there is no player-visible change to report.** **TK-01 not due, verified by listing `marketing/outbox/` myself:** newest is `ticker-digest-2026-07-26.md`; the 27th's coverage compiles **today ≥06:00 local** (it is 00:07). **ART slot untouched → staging audit not triggered**, stated rather than silently skipped. **Assayer `pending/` = 0 (listed, empty).** **DEPLOY SKIPPED, correctly: zero `src/` merged.** Backup push attempted after this handoff. ⚠️ Unchanged gap: `test:guards` still has **no CI caller**. 🧹 No scratch server left running — the playwright runs used the suite's own webServer on the verified-free 5188 and exited with the run; **I started no long-lived process and killed nothing by a remembered pid.** Four tracked helper scripts committed as evidence (`scripts/tmp-s1144-*.mjs|txt`) because the bash gate reads backticks and `$?` in inline `node -e`/compound commands as subshells. (G) **THE LESSON: s1143 learned that a stale ARTIFACT hides live regressions. This fire found the sibling failure mode — a stale NAME. A rename that lands correctly in `src/` and silently in nothing else does not announce itself; it decays into six separate "known reds" that each look individually reasonable to defer.** *When you meet a pre-existing red, ask what ELSE shares its root — and check the date on the review that called it green.*
