scripts/tmp-s1191-register-drain.mjs:24:  "ACCEPTED. THE PRE-DECLARED DECISIVE EXPERIMENT RAN AND IT FLIPPED, AND I RE-DERIVED EVERY PUBLISHED FIGURE INSTEAD OF READING THE TABLE. s1189's survey left Rail Tough diagonal rows 2/3 UNCERTAIN because two instruments disagreed: the bodies read as an nw/ne mirror pair while the 2v3 IoU was direct-dominant (+0.248), which reads as the same heading twice. s1190's master supplied the mechanism rather than just the doubt — every instrument used so far discards all but the outline, and the Rail Tough is the one character of the three carrying a large one-hand prop, so mirroring a TRUE body heading aligns the bodies but throws the wrench blob onto the opposite side, deflating the mirrored score and inflating the direct one. THE MASKED RE-RUN CONFIRMS EXACTLY THAT: 2v3 goes from 0.706117 direct / 0.456002 mirrored (delta +0.250115) to 0.705447 direct / 0.832448 mirrored (delta -0.127001). The direct score moves by -0.001 while the mirrored score gains +0.376 — a ONE-SIDED signature; a mask that merely shrank both scores would have proved nothing. Subject self-mirror floor 0.4524952. Not a mask-size coin flip: 9/9 sensitivity cases (shaft 10/12/14 x jaw 20/22/24) stay mirror-dominant, delta range -0.1176 to -0.1270. Rows 2 and 3 are a lawful nw/ne mirror pair; the duplicate-row hypothesis is dead. THE HARDER HALF, AND THE REASON THIS PASSED THE GATE s1190 SET: the run VALIDATED its locator on the known-good rows before pointing it at the disputed ones (diagonal rows 0/1 reproduce the published screen-left control: row 0 -69.5/-63.5/-52.8/-56.5, row 1 -62.4/-45.5/-56.7/-52.7; rows 2/3 are screen-RIGHT at +52.6/+59.8/+46.4/+53.7 and +59.3/+64.5/+58.3/+61.2) AND IT REJECTED A DISCRIMINATOR RATHER THAN FORCING A CONCLUSION FROM IT — the obvious cardinal cross-check fails, because the consumer's n row 3 keeps the wrench screen-LEFT (-46.6/-49.8/-50.4/-46.8) exactly like s row 0 (-63.6/-62.6/-66.0/-68.9), so cardinal wrench side carries no front/back information at all. The report labels that Confidence NONE as a body-side control, explains it (row-3 pixels expose face, chest and badge like a side/front turn rather than a back view), isolates it from the verdict and changes nothing in the asset or contract. A weaker run would have reported the cardinal agreement as corroboration. PROVENANCE PROVED BY HASH, NOT BY CLAIM: the probe is deterministic across two consecutive runs and its live stdout hashes byte-identical to the committed artifacts/eight-winds-rail-tough/probe-results.json (bdb7d8c6254f035fe67cc5d21639fed15a106cd0ee5a885e38e1f31752a5c7a9); both locator boards match their published SHA-256s (c1e7adc2..., 3d1112b2...). GATES on the merged tree: drain-block-check CLEAR run FIRST; tsc exit 0; build 1.58s asset-diet green; test:node-guards 61/61. NO PLAYWRIGHT, AND THAT IS PROPORTIONATE RATHER THAN A THINNED BAR: 39 files / 1110 insertions / 0 deletions, and a staged-path audit (not the runner's assertion) confirms zero paths outside artifacts/eight-winds-rail-tough/, the probe and the run report — nothing under src/, e2e/, assets/, scripts/ or any contract, so nothing renders and Mistake #10's honest answer is 'nowhere yet'. MERGE CLASSIFICATION: pure-add; all 39 files LANE-TOUCHED-ONLY and disjoint from main's concurrent bookkeeping moves (STATUS.md, tasks/BACKLOG.md, tasks/goals.json, tasks/lane-a-m3-05d-*.md, logs/*), so no 3-way graft; merged by path-scoped checkout of the three lane paths. TWO FINDINGS. F-1191-1 (non-blocking, and the one claim a green gate cannot check): the nw vs ne LABELS are one confidence tier below the PAIR — the report's own table says HIGH pair / MEDIUM label, but 'no diagonal row remains UNCERTAIN' should not be read as uniform certainty. Which row is nw and which is ne rests on the visual west/east read, because the decisive instrument is symmetric by construction — masking the prop is precisely what removes the information that could tell the pair apart. If wrong, rows 2/3 are swapped and the cure is a one-line contract swap with no regeneration; the E2 wiring slice's in-game review should check a north-west walk on camera, which settles the label more cheaply than any further pixel work. F-1191-2 (informational): logs/s1190-rail-tough-wrench-probe.mjs is a genuinely re-runnable, self-asserting, deterministic instrument that nothing calls — an unrun guard the moment this fire ends. Deliberately NOT wired into test:node-guards, because it reads artifacts/ scratch extractions that are not part of the shipped asset set and coupling the guard battery to scratch bytes would be the wrong cure. NET EFFECT: the E2 art request is now fully sized at 4 regenerated rows across three sheets (Coal Thief row 0 as sw; Steam Wrecker row 1 as lawful se with a SINGLE cyan tank per F-1189-2 and row 2 as lawful nw; Rail Tough row 1 as one stable se), so it ships as ONE request — which is exactly what s1190 declined to spend a 75%-sized batch on.";
