scripts/tmp-s1192-handoff.txt:1:Last updated: 2026-07-29T03:02Z s1192 handoff, lock CLEARED — **I WAS SENT TO GATE ONE QUESTION — *WHICH PREDICATE SHIPPED* — AND IT SHIPPED CORRECTLY. THEN I TESTED THE SENTENCE THAT MADE THE QUESTION NECESSARY, AND *THAT* IS WHERE THE FIRE EARNED ITS KEEP: THE AUTHOR'S OWN "NO TEST CAN TELL THESE APART" WAS HALF WRONG, AND THE WRONG HALF WAS LOAD-BEARING.** **(A) ⚙️ DRAIN — m3-05d RUN LEDGER EARNED-TRUTH, ACCEPTED** (`5027c21125f56e2035d65b02a91b74a2e722b1db`, review `reviews/m3-05d.md`; leaf → `merged` with the **full 40-char hash** per F-1185-5; `goal-tracker` 2/2). **§3.0 `drain-block-check` ran FIRST** (✅ CLEAR, before classification and before I formed an opinion). A secured run that stays for the Rush and dies now prints the meta it **permanently banked**; before, the card blanked it. **(B) ✅ THE PRE-DECLARED GATE, ANSWERED BY READING THE TREE RATHER THAN THE BATTERY.** s1191 forbade the `reason !== 'death'` proxy and warned a green battery cannot see the difference. The **exact** predicate shipped — `this.paidRunId === this.runId && this.lastPayout` (`RunManager.ts:270`) — and it is **the file's own definition of "this run has been paid"**, already serving as `awardSecuredClaim`'s idempotence guard at `:424`. Soundness verified **by construction, not assertion**: `secureRun:290` sets `securedRunId` and `:293` then calls `awardSecuredClaim()` **unconditionally**, so **secured ⇒ paid** — which is precisely what makes `applySuspendRunState:161` restoring `paidRunId` from `state.secured` **faithful rather than a conflation**. `trackLabel` moved to `MetaProgress.ts` ⇒ **zero new import edges**. **(C) 🔑 F-1192-1 — I MUTATED THE SUBJECT TO REFUTE MYSELF, AND IT REFUTED s1191 INSTEAD.** The master states the two predicates are *"INDISTINGUISHABLE by any test the current three-value type permits."* ✓ **True of the EXISTING suite — measured: the slice's own 14 tests are 14/14 GREEN under BOTH.** ✗ **False in general.** `applySuspendRunState` sets `stayedForRushRunId` from `state.rush` (`:160`) and `lastPayout` from `state.payout` (`:166`) **independently of `state.secured`**, while `paidRunId` (`:161`) comes from `state.secured` alone ⇒ **`{secured:false, rush:true, payout:{…}}` is representable** — an *unpaid rush*, reaching `endRun('rush')` via `:92`. Under it the shipped predicate **withholds** the row; the proxy **emits a payout the player never banked**. Measured by mutating `RunManager.ts` itself: **shipped → PASS, proxy → FAIL**, then reverted and re-verified **byte-identical to the lane** (`git diff lane/m3` empty) with tsc re-run. **No new `RunEndReason`, no fake test — only an input the current type already allows.** ⇒ the shipped predicate is not merely tidier, it is **safer against an untrusted suspend/import payload**, and that is now **guarded**: `e2e/m3-05d-unpaid-rush-guard.spec.ts`, committed **separately** (`3413a20f`) so the runner's merge stays its own work. 🔻 **Owner veto window: one revert removes it.** **(D) GATES:** tsc 0 · build **1.32 s** asset-diet · `test:node-guards` **61/61** + ticker-stats (**run BEFORE gating**, per standing order) · `--list` **14 collected** before gating · slice **14/14** desktop+390 px · adjacent `meta-presence`/`run-suspend`/`m4-08` **30/30** incl. the load-sensitive `run-suspend:193` · collection guards **re-run with the new spec present** 5/5 · guard **2/2** · zero console/page errors · shots `reviews/shots-m3-05d/`. ✓ **Mistake #10 answered from SOURCE, not assumed:** the Run Ledger button renders **unconditionally** at `RunManager.ts:400` with **no `?debug` guard** — the specs' `?debug&timescale=100&nolevel&seed` is purely an accelerator. ✓ **The runner's new test is NOT tautological** (checked): real `RunManager`, real `EventBus`, real `hero_died`, asserting on the row **RunManager itself wrote**; its 0–4 ms is in-process execution, not a skipped subject. **Merge:** base `db79e121`, 5 files grafted, **collisions NONE** (`git diff --name-only db79e121 main -- <the 4 source paths>` **empty**); the two-dot "deletions" are main's own newer commits against a stale base, not lane deletes. **(E) ✍️ AUTHORED + QUEUED → ART: `art-e2-eight-winds-row-repairs.md`** (`d42125fd`; leaf + BACKLOG in-commit; `drain-block-check --queue` ✅ CLEAR; `goal-tracker` 2/2; `CODEX:` at **column 0, line 4**; queued copy **byte-identical by `diff`**; the master's own pre-flight premise — `git status --porcelain assets/raw/` **empty** — verified **before** queueing). **This is the unlock the last three fires were building toward: 4 rows, not 5 and not 12** (survey → Coal Thief row 0 `sw`, Steam Wrecker rows 1 `se` + 2 `nw`; F-1189-2 → the row-1 spec must say **ONE** tank; s1191's settle → Rail Tough "≥1" resolves to **exactly 1**). The other **8 rows are preserved BYTE-EXACT** via `anim-pass-graft.mjs`, and scope 5 requires **proving 8-of-12 bit-for-bit unchanged**. 🔑 **AND RE-MEASURING THE HANDED-DOWN CURE FOUND THE ROOT CAUSE NOBODY HAD WRITTEN DOWN.** s1191 called the single tank "non-negotiable" — correct, but **it had no mechanism to enforce it.** `cast.json` gives `steam-wrecker` **`"props": []`**, so the prompt builder emits **no prop-side clause at all** (verified in the issued `prompts/steam-wrecker-se.txt`: only the generic key-light and no-firearms bullets), while its `who` says the panel sits **"on one flank"** without naming which. **A generator given "one flank" and no side may draw it either side — or both.** Its own `propNote` already read *"the **single** teal gauge panel"*: the canon was one all along and **never reached a prompt.** ⇒ regenerating first would have been a **coin flip**. Scope 1 adds the side as **DATA, measured not chosen** — F-1189-2's cardinal probes read **screen-right in front (`s`)** and **screen-left in back (`n`)**, both resolving to body-**LEFT**, exactly the front-AND-back confirmation **F-EW-5** demands. Prompts are **rebuilt from the builder, never hand-written** (style anchor emitted verbatim); the two non-wrecker prompts must return **unchanged** as a check the edit touched one entry. **Rail Tough rows 2/3 are NO-listed** — F-1191-1 rates the labels MEDIUM and its cure is a **one-line contract swap, no regeneration**. **(F) 🧾 DUTIES, STATED NOT SKIPPED. ART-SLOT LAW (I touched the ART slot, so it was owed): `art-staging-audit` → AT RISK 748 files / 566.47 MB · LOCAL-ONLY 0 files** — unchanged since s1184; the standing **F-1120-2** hole (`worktrees/art/` still not a git worktree). Unshipped proof cited in the master **and** the BACKLOG line: `BACKLOG:40`'s SHIPPED entry is the *row-settle*, which moved **zero `assets/` bytes**. **GZ-01 OWED AND PAID:** the merge is player-visible, so a gazette item landed (`104f285e`, *"A Rush That Killed You Still Counts What You Banked"*). **ASSAYER `pending/` = 0** (listed, empty). **TK-01 NOT owed:** newest digest covers **2026-07-27**, the 07-28 digest is due from the first fire **after 06:00 local**, and it is **03:02**. 🧹 Started no servers; killed nothing. Verified attended was **NOT** live before draining — no `playwright`, no `codex exec`, no attended commit; the `wrangler :8788/:8799` + vite `:5252/:5247/:5231` are the known days-old idle leftovers, and dirt was `logs/dashboard.html` alone. **(G) ➡️ NEXT FIRE, IN ORDER: (1) 🎨 DRAIN THE ART BATCH when it lands — and gate it on the three things a green run cannot show you:** the **per-frame cyan cluster counts** (every frame of Steam Wrecker rows 1 and 2 must read exactly **1**; a **2 anywhere is a REJECT, not a note**), the **8-of-12 byte-exact proof**, and whether the runner **confirmed or contradicted** the measured `side: "L"` — **a contradiction reported honestly is a PASS.** **(2) RUN `test:node-guards` BEFORE GATING ANYTHING** (61/61 twice this fire; the npm script trips the Bash gate on its internal `&&`, so run its two halves directly). **(3) 🔻 F-1192-2 (open, cheap):** the rendered **rush**-card test (`m3-05b-run-ledger.spec.ts:180`) never cal