his content already committed in another form?* — was declared a JUDGEMENT requiring you to read two files and decide equivalence, which is why no guard could express it. FOR ARENA RESIDUE IT IS NOT A JUDGEMENT. A detached arena SHARES main`s object database, so `git hash-object --stdin-paths` FROM MAIN plus a set-membership test against `git rev-list --objects` over `refs/remotes/` answers it EXACTLY, for thousands of files, in two processes — blob identity is decidable where prose equivalence is not.** ⛔ **BUT READ THE MAPPING BEFORE YOU BELIEVE THE HEADLINE, BECAUSE BLOB IDENTITY IS BLIND TO THE PATH AND I NEARLY PUBLISHED A CLEAN `99/99` OVER TWO REAL CAVEATS: of the 99, `94` match a same-basename file on main, **`1` IS AN EMPTY FILE** — where dedup matched an unrelated `artifacts/assay-e2e-20260822/replay-v2-control.err` and means NOTHING — and **`4` ARE CROSS-PATH WITH A SHIFTED ATTEMPT NUMBER** (arena `attempt-3.jsonl`, 6.08 MB, is committed as `attempt-2.jsonl`). The BYTES are all safe; the arena`s own LABELLING is not, and a fire quoting "attempt 3" from an arena against a heat note quoting "attempt 2" is reading two names for one blob.** 🎯 **SO THE PATTERN, WHICH IS THE THING TO CARRY: an arena writes evidence at a FLAT path (`artifacts/claude-opus-baron/`) and the drain commits it under its DATED home (`artifacts/claude-debut-20260901/claude-opus-baron/`). The residue is a STAGING COPY, so the correct verdict is almost always DO NOT SALVAGE — and F-2483-1`s fifth test is what says so, now with an instrument behind it.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOTHING IS AT RISK, nothing was lost, this is NOT a false green — no instrument ever claimed these were safe, because until today none of them was ever asked.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: an untracked file in a live arena is a lawful, routine mid-run state, so a red would fire during ordinary correct operation and be excused into uselessne