 `CLAUDE.md` **0** · `.claude/skills/author-task/SKILL.md` **0** · `.claude/skills/drain/SKILL.md` **0**; it appears only in `STATUS.md` handoff archives and `tasks/BACKLOG.md` findings prose, **the two surfaces F-1654-1 itself proved a refilling fire does not read at refill time.** So F-1654-1's own diagnosis — *"a measured refusal had nowhere to live"* — recurred one level up: **the refusal-READER had nowhere to live.** 💰 **Cost, paid by the fire that wrote this clause and not inherited from anyone: s2153 re-derived `jumper-8way-wiring`'s refusal BY HAND through six probes** — goal-tree status census → `master-shipped-classifier` → reading the master → grepping `assets/LEDGER.md` for the `char.claim_jumper SHEET full-ROTATION` row → `drain-block-check` → an `authoringBlock` census — to arrive at precisely the verdict s1661 had already recorded ON THE LEAF **eleven days earlier**, one command away. ⓘ **AND `drain-block-check` WILL NOT SAVE YOU HERE — IT PRINTS `✅ CLEAR` FOR BOTH BANKED MASTERS** (`lane-c-jumper-8way-wiring.md` and `lane-e3-fairground-socket.md`, verified s2153), and it is RIGHT to: it answers *may I DRAIN this?*, and a `planned` leaf has nothing to drain. **A CLEAR from the drain guard is not a licence to QUEUE** — the two questions have two instruments, and §3.0's tool is deliberately blind to `authoringBlock`. Its sibling `node scripts/master-shipped-classifier.mjs` answers the other half — *is this banked master already SHIPPED?* (Mistake #8, the 824k Flail) — and is likewise named in no law surface (`fire.md` 0 · `CLAUDE.md` 0 · `author-task/SKILL.md` 0, measured s2153). ⚠️ **AND RUN IT FROM THE MAIN WORKTREE — FROM A LANE IT USED TO INFLATE THE QUEUE-ME SET 268× AND SAY NOTHING (F-2222-2, measured s2222, CURED s2223).** Three of its four inputs are TRACKED (`tasks/*.md`, the trace dirs under `tasks/`, `tasks/goals.json`), so a linked worktree hands it a board FROZEN at that lane’s commit. It now REFUSES there (`⛔ CANNOT VERIFY — DO NOT QUEUE`,