lation path, so its green is not evidence about the red (the s1299/s1300 standard). s1301 truncated the live `verifiers-gate-and-stderr` hash to `818aa398`, reproducing s1300 exactly: **rc=1**, `AssertionError` naming `'818aa398'` against `/^[0-9a-f]{40}$/`; probe reverted, `goals.json` restored byte-identical. ⚠️ **Do not read the drain battery's green as covering your bookkeeping** — it was taken before the row existed, and no amount of care at that moment can change what the tree did not yet contain. ⓘ If the bash allowlist refuses the npm script name, run the same set through `node` directly (the gate denies YOU, not the factory) — that is how s1301 measured it.\012F. **Nothing to do**: exit clean — rewrite line-1 as a no-op handoff only if you took the lock; otherwise just exit. NEVER invent scope. 📋 **BUT EARN THE WORD "DRY" FIRST — `ls -1t tasks/done/ | head` IS NOT A DRAIN CHECK, AND IT IS STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE OF BECOMING ONE (F-2205-1, measured s2205; the cure was measured s1061 and sat 27 days in untracked memory with nowhere to live).** Closed done-moves are RENAMED with a prefix (`drained-` 327 · `shipped-` 149 · `janitor-` 84 · `stopped-` 82 · `noop-` 16 · 11 rarer spellings), and a rename re-stamps the file — so **every closed entry is newer than every undrained one, and the undrained ones are bare-dated (`20260818-200526-<task>.md`) and sort UNDERNEATH.** A newest-first peek therefore returns *only* closed work and **always looks clean**; the more diligently the factory renames, the blinder the probe gets. 📊 **Measured s2205: 1,353 done-moves, 676 bare-dated — 50.0%, i.e. HALF the corpus lives below the fold of `head`.** 💰 **THE INCIDENT: s1057, s1058, s1059 and s1060 EACH honestly reported "no drain exists" on this read; s1061 listed the un-prefixed ones and found `art-batch-roster-e10` UNDRAINED FOR 28 HOURS** — the last era's roster art, present only in untracked `worktrees/art/`, with `git ls-files` showing zero E10 enemy art on main while E6–E9