e every time. 🪞 **AND THE SHARPEST LESSON THIS FIRE PAID FOR CAME FROM MY OWN CONTROL, WHICH WAS SILENTLY VACUOUS FOR EXACTLY THE REASON THE FINDING IS ABOUT.** My first F-1274-2 neutrality run wrote the pre-cure script to `/tmp` and diffed it against the cured one; it reported **DIVERGED**, which I nearly recorded as a real behavioural difference. In fact `main()` **never ran**: macOS symlinks `/tmp` to `/private/tmp`, so the module-main guard `path.resolve(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)` was FALSE and the process exited **rc=0, stdout 0 B, stderr 0 B** — indistinguishable from the very silence under test. ➡️ **A CONTROL WHOSE FAILURE MODE IS SILENCE CANNOT BE DISTINGUISHED FROM THE SILENCE IT MEASURES: assert that the control arm PRODUCED something before believing what it says.** The corrected run guards its own validity first (*"pre-cure arm produced 20 lines — it really ran"*) and then reads NEUTRAL on both modes. ⚠️ **AND THE SWALLOW NEED NOT BE A `catch` AT ALL — A GUARD-KEYED EMPTY IS INVISIBLE TO EVERY CENSUS THIS STREAK HAS RUN, BY CONSTRUCTION (F-2218-1, measured and cured s2218 — the FIFTEENTH consecutive fire to find a live instance of F-2204-1's class).** Six consecutive framings have sharpened *which `catch` to look at* — s2212 `grep -c catch` (file-level) · s2213 spawn lexically inside a `try` · s2214 same-file wrapper · s2215 handler polarity LOUD vs SILENT · s2216 `spawnSync` never throws · s2217 enumeration vs classification. **Every one of them is keyed on a handler, so none of them can see a corpus that empties without anything throwing:** `existsSync(dir) ? readdirSync(dir) : []` — no exception, no handler, no census hit. That is s2216's own lesson (a catch-keyed census cannot see `spawnSync`) recurring on the axis s2217 opened, and it is why the ladder felt terminated when it was not. 📊 **Measured s2218 over `326` non-test `scripts/*.mjs`: `6` guard-keyed empty enumerations in `5` files** — `drain-block-check.mjs` (two sit