HOLDING RIGHT NOW now exits 1.** Until s2097 the duplicate-dispatch refusal (F-1322-1) sat inside the `if (queue)` block that this UNKNOWN branch exits *before* reaching, so it was **structurally inert for every master with no goal leaf — 532 of 1093 in `tasks/*.md`, 48.7%, measured s2097**. **PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING THE DEFECT, not by a green: two fixtures identical but for the leaf, same master, same `tasks/running/lane-b--<stamp>-<name>` — leaf present → rc=1 `⛔ ALREADY DISPATCHED`; leaf absent → rc=0, no refusal printed at all.** The check reads only `tasks/running/` and `tasks/done/` and needs nothing from the goal tree, so the lookup was never a precondition — only an accident of where the call sat. 💡 **The reusable half: this is F-1597-1's shape surviving the cure that names it.** That finding fixed exactly this fall-through for the BLOCKED arm and wrote the lesson down — *"would fall through to UNKNOWN and exit 0 — an affirmative-looking clearance"* — and nobody carried the reasoning across to the sibling arm four lines away. **When you cure a fall-through, ask which OTHER checks sit behind the same early exit.** ⓘ The UNDRAINED WARN deliberately still does NOT fire on this path: it is the heuristic *"un-prefixed = never drained"*, 403 unregistered masters have a matching bare done-move, and with no leaf there is no ledger to test the heuristic against — a warning that is usually false on the majority path is how a guard decays into a formality. Re-measured s1276 on `003-vp-03-terrain-variety.md`: default **rc=0**, `--strict` **rc=2**, identical UNKNOWN text both times. A fire that branches on the exit code alone therefore reads UNKNOWN as permission — the precise failure §3.0 exists to prevent. Pass **`--strict`** if you want UNKNOWN to be rc=2, or parse the verdict text. 🚫 **The default is deliberately advisory and must NOT be flipped**: **541 of 1093 masters (49.5%, RE-MEASURED s2100** — was `538 of 941 (57.2%)` s1538, `526 of 762 (69.0%)` s1276, and `~76%` before that**)** have no leaf, so a strict default would red the whole board rather than the one master you are asking about. 📉 **THE RATIO IS FALLING AND THAT IS THE MEASUREMENT'S REAL CONTENT, SO READ THE DIRECTION, NOT THE HEADLINE (F-1538-1).** Across s1276→s1538 the ABSOLUTE debt barely moved (526→538, **+12**) while the denominator grew by **179** — so **167 of 179 new masters (93.3%) were registered**, and the Goal Registration Law is demonstrably WORKING. The unregistered set is legacy debt, now decaying by dilution at roughly 4.5 points per 180 masters. 🔔 **THAT WATCH-THRESHOLD HAS NOW BEEN CROSSED, AND THE SENTENCE THE POLICY RESTED ON IS FALSE — RE-MEASURED s2100 (F-2100-1).** This clause used to read *"a 57.2% majority still lacks leaves, so a strict default still reds the board"*, and set itself a trigger: *"the number to watch is when this crosses below ~50% — at that point the advisory-default argument stops being about 'most of the board' and needs restating on its merits rather than on the count. Do not flip it early because the trend is pretty."* **Both halves have now come due: 49.5% is NOT a majority, so the justification is factually dead, and the trigger condition is met.** 📅 **It crossed at `176268426` (2026-08-20T15:12:39+07:00) — 541/1084 = 49.91%, with the immediately preceding commit at exactly 50.00% (541/1082)** — about 11 hours and 105 first-parent commits before s2100, during ordinary attended bookkeeping, which is why no fire noticed. ⚖️ **THE POLICY SURVIVES, BUT ON A RESTATED ARGUMENT — WHICH IS PRECISELY WHAT THE TRIGGER ASKED FOR, AND IS NOT A FLIP:** a strict default would still red **541 masters**, i.e. **half the board rather than the one master you are asking about**, so the advisory default now stands on the **ABSOLUTE COUNT** and no longer on "most of the board." 🚫 **DO NOT FLIP IT** — the restatement is the discharge of the trigger, not a licence to change the default. 📈 **AND THE NEWS UNDER THE NEWS IS BETTER THAN s1538 RECORDED: across s1538→s2100 the denominator grew +152 while the ABSOLUTE debt grew +3 — so 149 of 152 new masters (98.0%) were registered**, up from 93.3% over s1276→s1538. **It crossed by DILUTION, exactly the mechanism F-1538-1 predicted**: the debt is frozen legacy (538→541 in 152 masters), and the ratio falls because the Goal Registration Law keeps working. **The next number to watch is the ABSOLUTE 541** — if it starts climbing, registration has stopped working and that is a different finding entirely. ✅ **WATCHED AT LAST, s2182 (F-2182-1) — 82 fires after this clause set the trigger, and it is NOT TRIPPED: the absolute is STILL 541, at `541/1122 = 48.2%`.** Denominator +29 since s2100, absolute **+0**. 🔑 **AND THE SET IS FROZEN, NOT MERELY THE COUNT — WHICH IS THE STRONGER FACT AND THE ONE A COUNT CANNOT ESTABLISH: 0 masters newly unregistered, 0 retroactively registered, 0 removed.** An equal count is also what a deletion plus an unregistered addition looks like; the set diff is what discriminates, so **ask for the diff, not the tally, whenever a watch-number holds still.** 📈 **All 29 new masters registered = 100.0%**, up from 98.0% (s1538→s2100) and 93.3% (s1276→s1538) — the Registration Law is working *better* each window, and the debt is inert legacy decaying purely by dilution, exactly as F-1538-1 predicted and this clause restated. **Re-measure the ABSOLUTE, not the ratio; carry the trigger forward unchanged.** ⓘ **METHOD CONTROLLED AGAINST THREE HISTORICAL TREES BEFORE ANY DRIFT WAS ASSERTED — WIDENED TO FIVE s2182, ALL REPRODUCED TO THE DIGIT** (s1276 `527/763 = 69.1%` · s1538 `538/941 = 57.2%` · the crossing commit `176268426` `541/1084 = 49.9%` · s2100 `541/1093 = 49.5%` · s2097 `541/1093`) (`git ls-tree <rev>:tasks` × that rev's own `goals.json`, matching `taskFile` EXACTLY): at s1538's tree it reproduces **538/941 = 57.2% to the digit**, at s1276's **527/763 = 69.1%** against a recorded 526/762 (±1, one boundary master). ⚠️ **At s2097's tree it yields 541/1093 where that fire recorded 532/1093** — denominator identical to the digit, numerator +9 — so s2097 almost certainly resolved leaves through `drain-block-check`'s SUBSTRING match, which matches more leaves and therefore reports fewer unregistered. **Both readings put the ratio below 50%, so the threshold verdict does not depend on which resolution is preferred**; the +9 is named here so the next fire re-measuring this does not mistake a method difference for a real jump. ⛔ **THAT "almost certainly" IS NOW MEASURED FALSE — REFUTED s2182 (F-2182-1), AND THE SENTENCE IS KEPT ONLY SO THE REFUTATION HAS A SUBJECT.** Replicating `drain-block-check`'s resolver EXACTLY (`:234–257` — `normalize()` then bidirectional substring, then the `leaf.id` fallback) at s2097's OWN tree yields **478/1093, not 532** — delta **63**, not 9. Two intermediate candidates miss it too: `normalize()`-equality **539**, `normalize()`+id-equality **536**. **No candidate method reproduces 532; its true derivation is UNRECOVERED**, and naming a mechanism for it was a guess wearing a measurement's clothes. ⚖️ **THE PRACTICAL CAUTION SURVIVES AND IS UNDERSTATED SEVENFOLD, WHICH IS THE HALF THAT MATTERS: the method-variance band at ONE FIXED TREE is 478–541 — 63 wide, not 9.** So *"do not mistake a method difference for a real jump"* is not merely right, it is **more** right than it claimed: a method swap can move this number by more than the entire legacy debt has moved in 900 fires. 💡 **REUSABLE: a hedge that names a MECHANISM invites the next fire to trust the mechanism and stop measuring; a hedge that names the measured BAND protects them.** When you cannot identify the cause of a divergent reading, publish the spread — not a plausible story. **Always re-derive with the EXACT-basename method above, which is the one controlled against four trees.** ⛔ **AND ROUTE IT THROUGH `node` — THE PRESCRIBED METHOD'S OWN INSTRUMENT IS REFUSED BY YOUR PERMISSION GATE (F-2427-1, measured s2427).** The