x — so they are not owed a fallback at all; recorded only so the next reader does not re-measure them.** 📉 **AND THE WATCH ITSELF IS DISCHARGED, 245 FIRES AFTER s2182 (F-2427-2): `539 / 1198 = 45.0%` — the ABSOLUTE **FELL BY 2** (541 → 539) while the denominator grew **+76**, so the trigger (*"if it starts climbing, registration has stopped working"*) is **NOT TRIPPED** and the sequence 69.1% → 57.2% → 49.9% → 48.2% → **45.0%** continues to fall by dilution exactly as F-1538-1 predicted. **Instrument validated against TWO recorded trees before its answer was believed (F-2215-1): the crossing commit `176268426` reproduces `541/1084 = 49.9%` and s2182's own tree `b4c797684` reproduces `541/1122` — both to the digit.** 🔑 **THE SET DIFF, which F-2182-1 rightly demands whenever the number moves: 76 new masters, 0 removed, **3 legacy debts RETIRED** (`ap-orders-adapter-wiring.md`, `art-batch-roster-e9.md`, `art-e9-buildings-a.md` — **precisely the three UNKNOWNs F-2206-1 and F-2208-1 resolved by file probe**, so the debt F-2208-1 warned would red `dry-board-probe --strict` at rc=2 is now genuinely gone, corroborated by this fire's own probe reading `UNKNOWN: 0`), and exactly ONE newly-unregistered master — `e3-fairground-socket.md`. ⚖️ **THAT ONE IS NOT A VIOLATION AND MUST NOT BE COUNTED AS ONE: it is a bannered SUPERSEDED duplicate whose taskFile key an attended session REMOVED ON PURPOSE the same day it was written (`note_s_att_20260823`, readable via `drain-block-check`), retained under the RETENTION LAW because we supersede rather than erase. Real registration is 76/76.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a measured LIMIT of this watch's own instrument: an exact-basename census scores a LAWFULLY leafless artifact as debt, so the ABSOLUTE can rise by one for a correct reason. A `+1` is a prompt to read the master, never a verdict that registration failed — ask `drain-block-check` before you alarm.** `--all` audits every blocked leaf on the board. ⏳ **AND RUN IT ONE STEP EARLIER IN TIME THAN THIS CLAUSE SAYS — BEFORE YOU WRITE A NEXT-FIRE INSTRUCTION THAT ASSERTS A TASK'S CLOSURE STATE, NOT MERELY BEFORE YOU DRAIN IT (F-1669-1, measured s1669).** This section's trigger is *the drain*, so it never fires for the fire that has nothing to drain — and that is exactly the fire that writes the handoff telling its successor what to drain. **s1665 asserted that `f1643-2` was a `gate-side` hold, citing as its evidence the DONE-MOVE FILENAME `stopped-s1655-gate-side-…`; s1667 and s1668 each copied the assertion forward.** The block had been lifted by **s1657 `9a32d94f2`**, whose diff deletes `status:"blocked"`, deletes `blockClass:"gate-side"`, deletes `blockedReason`, writes `status:"queued"` and **dispatches the master** — 1h52m after that filename froze. 🪦 **A done-move filename is minted once at done-move time and is NEVER renamed: it is a fossil of a claim the ledger can reverse, and here it did.** Measured across `tasks/done/`: **6 of 1270 filenames carry a closure-class token, 5 resolve to a leaf, and 2 of those 5 (40%) are contradicted by their live leaf** — this one (`queued`), and `…s1176-blocked-by-26-cell-master-divergence-…-eight-winds-wiring-hero.md`, whose leaf reads `merged` at `29bac3d9478e9f3a77385c75965b60447a90500c`. ⚠️ **The cost is not a stale paragraph — it is an armed Silent No-Op (Mistake #1):** the stopped run that filename names **left zero diff** by its own preserved record, so a successor obeying the instruction gates a run that changed nothing, and looks for a `blocked` leaf to flip that does not exist. 🚫 **No mechanism is proposed and the reason is the point: the obvious one — have this tool print the filename-vs-leaf disagreement — is cheap and purely mechanical and STILL would not have prevented this, because s1665 never ran the tool.** It had the filename in hand and read its words. **A tool only helps the fire that asks it** (the F-1582-1 gap: the misread happens while a fire reads with its eyes, a moment no battery