git ls-files --others --exclude-standard -- artifacts/` selects on **LOCATION** (`-- artifacts/`), on **TRACKED-NESS** (`--others`, correct) and on **IGNORE STATUS** (`--exclude-standard`) — and the location key was narrower than the finding's own rationale, which cites `review-evidence-audit.mjs:55` where `EVIDENCE_PREFIXES = ['artifacts', 'reviews/shots-']` declares **TWO** sinks. `CLAUDE.md` §4.1 names them in one breath — *"screenshots in `reviews/shots-*/` or `artifacts/`"* — **so the LAW treats the two sinks as INTERCHANGEABLE and the IGNORE FILE did not:** `.gitignore:7` is a repo-wide `*.log` whose F-1573-1 negation at `:74` covers `artifacts/**` and had **no sibling for `reviews/shots-*`**. 📊 **PROVED BY MANUFACTURING, ground truth = each dir holding ONLY a run log, which is the real drain-evidence shape: `artifacts/…/run.log` RETAINED · `reviews/shots-…/run.log` SWALLOWED — invisible to `git status --short` (ZERO lines), invisible to the triage read above (wrong prefix), and invisible to that read WIDENED to `reviews/` as well, because `--exclude-standard` drops an ignored path outright.** Four instruments, one file, no report from any of them. ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: LATENT, and the class is EMPTY in the whole history — 0 tracked `*.log` under `reviews/shots-*` (all 71 tracked logs under `reviews/` are the eight-winds codex banners at `:60`), 0 untracked, 0 ignored-but-present. NOTHING HAS EVER BEEN LOST HERE.** What earns it a clause is that the identical mechanism one directory over **already cost f1572-1 its 24 run logs** (F-1573-1's own comment), and that the two sinks are interchangeable BY LAW — so a runner told to write evidence to one of them retains its log and to the other loses it silently. 🛠️ **CURE: `!reviews/shots-**/*.log`, mirroring `:74`. BLAST RADIUS MEASURED BEFORE LANDING, not assumed — it newly tracks ZERO files today and is purely forward-looking, exactly as `:74` and `gate-*/` were.** 🔬 **AND SCO