d/` · 1 `skills-lock.json` · 1 `tasks/` — five lines of output, and it cannot be aimed wrong.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: an untracked file is a LAWFUL routine mid-run state, so a red fires during ordinary correct operation and is excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1). This stays a triage READ, and the judging rule above is unchanged — never bulk-add what it returns.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the rung UNDER F-2358-1's own lesson: that finding said *enumerate every key your cure selects on*. It enumerated three and questioned one — the WIDTH of the location key. The sharper question is not HOW WIDE a selector is but WHETHER ITS AXIS CAN EXPRESS THE DEFECT AT ALL. A prefix names the places you thought of; the artifacts that hurt you are the ones nobody MEANT to write, and those have no place to be.** 🌳 **AND ASK IT IN EVERY WORKING TREE, NOT ONLY THIS ONE — THAT READ IS PER-WORKTREE BY CONSTRUCTION, AND §2H MANDATES WRITING EVIDENCE INTO A TREE IT CANNOT SEE (F-2484-1, measured and cured s2484).** `git ls-files --others` reports on the working tree it is RUN IN, so the repo-wide read above — at any pathspec width, including none — is complete over main and **structurally blind to every other working tree of this same repo**. §2H tells every heat to build a **DETACHED ARENA** (`git worktree add --detach`), and a heat writes its primary evidence there. 📊 **LIVE INSTANCE, s2484: `/tmp/heat11-5e7a7c0b/artifacts/heat11/` — `80` files, `11.8 MB`, untracked, in NO object database: every controller, tape, `gauntlet-outcome.json` and `gauntlet-report.md` for BOTH rigs across ALL THREE maps of heat 11. Main’s own repo-wide sweep returned `49` files that same minute and named none of them — CORRECTLY, because they are not in main’s tree.** 🔍 **AND NO OTHER INSTRUMENT REACHES IT EITHER, verified by READING rather than assumed: `art-staging-audit` scans art staging and its honest NOT-AUDITED list names only the four trees under