nd under-counts spawns routed through a wrapper; it was validated first by returning ZERO for all three already-bounded files.** ✅ **EXECUTED s2430 FOR THE `test:ledger-guards` HALF — 83 sites across 61 legs — AND THE COUNT WAS RE-DERIVED RATHER THAN INHERITED, WHICH FOUND THREE CORRECTIONS, TWO OF THEM IN THE DIRECTION THAT MANUFACTURES WORK (F-2430-1). ⛔ DO NOT WORK FROM THE `160`: (1) TRAILING COMMAS** — `spawnSync(a, b, {...},\n)` splits a final whitespace-only argument, and reading THAT as the options bag scores an **already-bounded** site as unbounded; **13 phantom sites in `gr-sim.test.mjs` alone, every one already carrying `timeout: 30_000`.** **(2) SYNC vs ASYNC, the load-bearing one, and it was never in the key: the mechanism REQUIRES a SYNCHRONOUS spawn, because the entire harm is that the event loop is blocked.** An async `spawn`/`exec`/`execFile`/`fork` leaves the loop free, so `--test-timeout` and any per-test `{ timeout }` **DO** fire and the wedge is already LOUD — **24 node-child sites are async and NOT exposed, including all four surviving `gr-sim.test.mjs` sites.** **(3) SPAWNERS NAMED IN PROSE** — this repo's guards carry long headers that QUOTE code, so a bare regex counts `execFileSync('npm', …)` inside a `/* … */` block as a call site (measured at `law-bash-prescription-guard.test.mjs:33`); **45 phantom sites.** 📊 **TRUE FIGURES: `143` exposed repo-wide before the cure, `60` after; inside mandated battery legs `123` → `28`.** 🧰 **AND IT IS NO LONGER PROSE — ASK THE INSTRUMENT: `node scripts/spawn-bound-census.mjs [--list] [--strict --max=N]`,** which derives the battery legs from `package.json` (F-2207-1), declares its corpus on stdout always (F-2208-1), anchors to `import.meta.url` (F-2220-1), resolves EXTRACTED `const` option bags — the exact key s2429 declined a guard for being unable to handle — and is advisory by default for F-1460-1's reason. 📐 **THE BOUND VALUE IS A MEASUREMENT, AND s2428's DOES NOT GENERALISE: both mandated batteries run at `--test-timeout=300_000` and the slowest known battery test is `fixture-teardown`'s at 69.6 s (F-2099-1), so the `60_000` s2428 used is BELOW the slowest lawful observation and would red a lawful leg. Use `240_000`.** ⛔ **AMENDED s2465 (F-2465-2) — `240_000` IS A DEFAULT, NOT A CONSTANT, AND APPLYING IT MECHANICALLY TO THE VERY TEST THIS SENTENCE CITES WOULD RED A LAWFUL RUN.** The `69.6 s` above is **RESTATED, NOT DELETED** — it was honest at s2099 — but it has drifted the way every figure in this clause drifts: `fixture-teardown` spawned **34** subjects then and **116** now. **RE-MEASURED s2465 by replicating its exact method: the sum of its children is `869.9 s`, and ONE child — `gr-sim.test.mjs`, run ALONE with an isolated `TMPDIR` and no bound — is `326.2 s` at `status=0`, `22 tests / 20 pass / 0 fail`.** So `fixture-teardown.test.mjs:35`'s spawn has a slowest LAWFUL observation of **326.2 s**, i.e. **above** the house bound, and binding it at `240_000` is F-1410-2 in the opposite costume: curing a hang by shrinking the bound until honest work fails. ⓘ **`--test-timeout` cannot save you either, and that is F-2429-1's own mechanism restated: `spawnSync` BLOCKS THE EVENT LOOP, so the outer timer can never fire.** ➡️ **THEREFORE, BINDING: size a bound against the slowest lawful child of THAT spawn, re-measured, never inherited. `240_000` remains right for a short-lived CLI child (which is 8 of the 9 sites F-2465-1 surfaced); a spawn whose child is itself a full battery needs its own measurement and generous headroom.** 💡 **REUSABLE: a house constant is a measurement someone took on a different subject. When a law hands you a number AND names the observation it came from, check that the observation still describes the thing you are about to apply it to.** ⚖️ **THE `28` ARE DISCHARGED — s2432 PAID EXACTLY THE COST THIS SENTENCE NAMED AS ITS REASON FOR DEFERRING (F-2436-1, see the re-verification above).** It read *"THE REMAINING `28` ARE `test:node-guards`-ONL