row as law/ledger/gate surfaces do, so COUNT it, never PRUNE it back to the number written here.** ⚠️ **AND A LEAF OF THAT BATTERY CAN MAKE A UNIVERSAL CLAIM OVER A CORPUS IT NEVER COUNTED — THE SWALLOW NEED NOT BE A `catch` OR A GUARD, IT CAN BE THE CWD (F-2220-1, measured and cured s2220 — the SEVENTEENTH consecutive fire to find a live instance of F-2204-1’s class).** `nul-audit.mjs` prints `CLEAN — no raw NUL bytes in tracked text sources`: a claim about **every** tracked text source, from a corpus built by `git ls-files`, which is **CWD-RELATIVE**. From a subdirectory it lists only that subtree, so the scan silently narrows and still prints CLEAN. **Nothing throws, no handler exists, and no guard is keyed on anything** — so every census in this lineage (s2212–s2219, `catch`-keyed then guard-keyed) was structurally incapable of seeing it. 📊 **PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING on a scratch repo whose ground truth was ONE NUL-bearing tracked file, control asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1): from the repo root → `1 file(s) carry raw NUL bytes`, rc=1, the file named; from `scripts/` → `CLEAN`, rc=0 — BYTE-IDENTICAL on stdout, stderr AND rc to the REVERSE CONTROL, a genuinely clean board. A third arm (the NUL file tracked but unreadable) is byte-identical too.** 🎯 **AND THE SIBLING IS NOT LATENT AT ALL — IT DIVERGES ON THE LIVE BOARD, TODAY: `attended-owed-audit.mjs` keys on the bare relative `tasks/attended-owed`, so from the repo root it reports `1 item(s): 1 open` (a 21-day-old attended-owed item) and from `scripts/` it reports `CLEAN — 0 item(s)` at rc=0 — and `--strict` exits 0 there where it should exit 1.** Same binary, same board, ninety seconds apart. ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY: in the PRESCRIBED invocation both are sound and every `CLEAN` this battery has printed was TRUE — verified, not assumed (measured s2220: `nul-audit` reads 9,701 of 9,709 text subjects, 8 empty, ZERO swallowed). `test:ledger-guards` runs under npm, whose cwd is always the package ro