RECURRING TRIGGER: the destination is `tasks/queue/main/`, the runner dispatches whatever lands there with NO shipped-check of its own (its single `drain-block-check` mention is a COMMENT at `lane-runner-v3.sh:391` — verified by reading, not grepped), and §2E's independent trigger *"re-queue paused main items (queue-paused/) once the pile is below 2"* fires on EVERY dry board, today's included (pile 0). That is Mistake #8 — the 824k Flail, this catalog's most expensive recorded failure — one `mv` away, with a stale instruction pointing at it.** ➡️ **THE STANDING RULE THAT REPLACES IT: `queue-paused/` is NOT a resume queue, it is a PARKING LOT whose occupants change. Before moving anything out of it, run `node scripts/drain-block-check.mjs <master> --queue` and obey the verdict — the directory being non-empty is not evidence that its contents are owed.** ⓘ **The parked file is deliberately LEFT AS s2382 NAMED IT: it is untracked scratch, and renaming it would erase another fire's own labelling of its own finding (supersede, never erase).** 💡 **REUSABLE: a standing order that names its subjects in PROSE but selects them with a GLOB is two different instructions, and only the prose expires legibly. When you retire the last item a wildcard was written for, retire the wildcard in the same breath — otherwise it silently re-aims at whatever next occupies the directory, and the newcomer inherits an authority nobody granted it.**\012- Robin owes (nag politely in handoffs, never block on it): lane-d attempt-3 verdict (3a recommended), turret-feel + water-feel playtests, Mac full-regression evidence, favicon 16px eyeball.\012- Canon guardrails always: brief §9 (no firearms — frontier-tech only; illustrated never gory; no Native American enemies; naming per §9.4; the agent is "the Prospector").\012\012## GZ-01 + TK-01 DUTIES (added 2026-07-10, attended — the news pipeline goes live)\012ON EVERY REAL-CHANGE MERGE ON MAIN — **whoever landed it, not only the ones you drain** (the filter law is unchanged: the review names a player-visible change): APPEND a news item to marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md. 🔑 **RE-KEYED s1546 FROM THE DRAINER TO THE MERGE EVENT (F-1546-1).** The old wording read "every real-change merge **you drain**", which keys the duty on the AGENT — and the factory's drain load has moved to attended sessions, so the pipeline was simply never *entered* when a human drained. Measured: **four player-visible slices merged attended-side on the morning of 2026-08-08 (`99f0d60a40…` f-door-1, `38615d7841…` f-door-2, `5698e6ae30…` f-bal-1, `3dec093294…` mp-07b) — all four with review files, all four with ZERO news items**, while all twelve most-recent touches of the queue file were fires at drain time. Nothing in the pipeline was broken; the trigger just never fired. ➡️ **THEREFORE, AS A STANDING SWEEP: any fire backfills any real-change merge whose review exists and whose hash is absent from `gazette-queue.md`** (`grep` the hash — that is the whole check, and it costs one command). ⚠️ **BUT GREP THE 8-CHAR SHORT HASH ACROSS THE WHOLE OF `marketing/outbox/`, NEVER THE FULL HASH AGAINST `gazette-queue.md` ALONE — THE PIPELINE HAS TWO OWNER-FACING SINKS AND THE PRESCRIBED CHECK IS STRUCTURALLY BLIND TO ONE OF THEM (F-1600-1, measured s1600).** The daily TK-01 ticker digest below reaches the owner exactly as a GAZETTE item does, so a merge headlined there is REPORTED, not owed. 📐 **The two sinks cite hashes in DISJOINT conventions, which is what makes the blindness categorical rather than a sampling artifact — measured across the live outbox: ticker digests carry 618 short hashes and ZERO full-40 ones, while `gazette-queue.md` carries 86 full and 105 short.** A full-40 grep therefore *cannot* match a ticker digest in principle, no matter how many fires run it. 📊 **Cost of the narrow check, window 2026-08-05→s1600: 81 player-path-touching first-parent merges, of which the narrow check calls 47 ABSENT — 20 of those are headlined in a ticke